        "dateAdded": "2026-05-20T06:32:22.639Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:26.51] Mississippi in the middle of a dry spell\n[00:31.75] Jimmie Rodgers on the Victrola up high\n[00:37.01] Mama's dancin' with a baby on her shoulder\n[00:41.98] The sun is settin' like molasses in the sky\n[00:47.46] The boy could sing, knew how to move, everything\n[00:53.48] Always wanting more, he'd leave you longing for\n[00:57.84] Black velvet and that little boy's smile\n[01:03.18] Black velvet with that slow southern style\n[01:08.92] A new religion that'll bring ya to your knees\n[01:13.65] Black velvet if you please\n[01:18.03] \n[01:27.26] Up in Memphis, the music's like a heatwave\n[01:32.91] White lightning, bound to drive you wild\n[01:37.85] Mama's baby's in the heart of every schoolgirl\n[01:42.75] \"Love Me Tender\" leaves 'em cryin' in the aisle\n[01:48.33] The way he moved, it was a sin, so sweet and true\n[01:53.68] Always wanting more, he'd leave you longing for\n[01:58.44] Black velvet and that little boy's smile\n[02:03.19] Black velvet with that slow southern style\n[02:09.72] A new religion that'll bring ya to your knees\n[02:14.44] Black velvet if you please\n[02:18.98] \n[02:23.28] Every word of every song that he sang was for you\n[02:30.29] \n[02:34.05] In a flash, he was gone, it happened so soon\n[02:41.73] What could you do?\n[02:45.84] \n[03:05.03] Black velvet and that little boy's smile\n[03:10.48] Black velvet with that slow southern style\n[03:15.75] A new religion that'll bring ya to your knees\n[03:20.75] Black velvet if you please\n[03:26.17] Black velvet and that little boy's smile\n[03:31.62] Black velvet with that slow southern style\n[03:36.61] A new religion that'll bring ya to your knees\n[03:42.11] Black velvet if you please\n[03:49.47] \n[03:57.14] If you please\n[03:59.92] \n[04:07.96] If you please\n[04:12.16] \n[04:17.52] If you please\n[04:18.32]",
