        "fullLyrics": "[00:17.39] Born down in a dead man's town\n[00:20.75] The first kick I took was when I hit the ground\n[00:25.02] You end up like a dog that's been beat too much\n[00:28.22] 'Til you spend half your life just covering up\n[00:33.69] Born in the U.S.A.\n[00:36.58] I was\n[00:37.65] Born in the U.S.A.\n[00:40.46] I was\n[00:41.45] Born in the U.S.A.\n[00:45.45] Born in the U.S.A. now\n[00:49.40] I got in a little hometown jam\n[00:53.77] So they put a rifle in my hands\n[00:57.02] Sent me off to a foreign land\n[01:01.68] To go and kill the yellow man\n[01:05.54] Born in the U.S.A.\n[01:08.38] I was\n[01:09.31] Born in the U.S.A.\n[01:12.54] I\n[01:13.42] Born in the U.S.A.\n[01:16.31] I was\n[01:17.37] Born in the U.S.A.\n[01:21.06] Come back home to the refinery\n[01:24.15] Hiring man says, \"Son, if it was up to me\"\n[01:29.31] Went down to see my V.A. man\n[01:32.67] He said, \"Son, don't you understand?\" now\n[01:52.63] I had a brother at Khe Sahn\n[01:56.50] Fighting off the Vietcong\n[02:00.44] They're still there, he's all gone\n[02:08.12] He had a woman in Saigon\n[02:11.97] I got a picture of him in her arms now\n[02:24.29] Down in the shadow of the penitentiary\n[02:26.71] Out by the gas fires of the refinery\n[02:31.32] I'm ten years down the road\n[02:35.13] Nowhere to run and got nowhere to go\n[02:39.53] Born in the U.S.A\n[02:42.40] I was\n[02:43.39] Born in the U.S.A\n[02:46.86] Born in the U.S.A\n[02:50.07] I'm a long gone daddy in the U.S.A.\n[02:55.94] Born in the U.S.A.\n[02:59.22] Born in the U.S.A\n[03:03.07] Born in the U.S.A\n[03:05.82] I'm a cool rocking daddy in the U.S.A. Now\n[03:11.03]",
