        "dateAdded": "2026-04-16T21:31:36.162Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:16.08] I was eight years old and running with a dime in my hand\n[00:24.07] Into the bus stop to pick up a paper for my old man\n[00:32.45] I'd sit on his lap in that big old Buick, steer as we drove through town\n[00:40.53] Tousle my hair, say, \"Son, take a good look around\"\n[00:48.44] This is your hometown\n[00:53.00] This is your hometown\n[00:56.88] This is your hometown\n[01:01.14] This is your hometown\n[01:09.79] In '65 tension was running high at my high school\n[01:17.33] Was a lot of fights 'tween the black and white, there was nothing you could do\n[01:25.78] Two cars at a light on a Saturday night, in the backseat there was a gun\n[01:33.42] Words were passed, shotgun blast, troubled times had come\n[01:42.06] To my hometown\n[01:45.76] To my hometown\n[01:50.16] To my hometown\n[01:54.22] To my hometown\n[02:02.55] Now Main Street's whitewashed windows and vacant stores\n[02:09.93] Seems like there ain't nobody wants to come down here no more\n[02:17.62] They're closing down the textile mill 'cross the railroad tracks\n[02:25.85] Foreman says, \"These jobs are going, boys, and they ain't coming back\"\n[02:34.91] To your hometown\n[02:39.20] Your hometown\n[02:42.92] To your hometown\n[02:47.13] To your hometown\n[02:55.94] Last night me and Kate, we laid in bed talking 'bout getting out\n[03:02.99] Packing up our bags, maybe heading south\n[03:11.49] I'm 35, we got a boy of our own now\n[03:19.27] Last night I sat him up behind the wheel and said \"Son, take a good look around\"\n[03:30.06] This is your hometown\n[03:35.60]",
        "genre": [
            "Rock"
        ],
