        "dateAdded": "2026-06-21T09:00:36.850Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:16.96] I come from down in the valley\n[00:21.17] Where, mister, when you're young\n[00:25.31] They bring you up to do\n[00:29.68] Like your daddy done\n[00:33.16] Me and Mary, we met in high school\n[00:37.71] When she was just 17\n[00:41.93] We'd drive out of this valley\n[00:45.71] Down to where the fields were green\n[00:51.77] We'd go down to the river\n[00:56.39] And into the river we'd dive\n[00:59.49] Oh-oh, down to the river we'd ride\n[01:06.46] \n[01:08.60] Then I got Mary pregnant\n[01:12.42] And, man, that was all she wrote\n[01:16.63] And for my 19th birthday\n[01:20.08] I got a union card and a wedding coat\n[01:24.95] We went down to the courthouse\n[01:28.64] And the judge put it all to rest\n[01:32.90] No wedding day smiles, no walk down the aisle\n[01:37.39] No flowers, no wedding dress\n[01:40.22] That night we went down to the river\n[01:45.48] And into the river we'd dive\n[01:48.95] Oh-oh, down to the river we did ride, ay-ay-ay\n[01:57.64] \n[02:32.72] I got a job, working construction\n[02:36.51] For the Johnstown Company\n[02:40.83] But lately there ain't been much work\n[02:44.39] On account of the economy\n[02:48.97] Now all them things that seemed so important\n[02:52.65] Well, mister, they vanished right into the air\n[02:56.54] Now I just act like I don't remember\n[03:00.81] Mary acts like she don't care\n[03:04.95] But I remember us riding in my brother's car\n[03:08.90] Her body tan and wet down at the reservoir\n[03:13.48] At night on them banks I'd lie awake\n[03:17.16] And pull her close just to feel each breath she'd take\n[03:21.28] Now those memories come back to haunt me\n[03:25.54] They haunt me like a curse\n[03:29.68] Is a dream a lie if it don't come true\n[03:34.02] Or is it something worse?\n[03:36.95] That sends me down to the river\n[03:41.66] Though I'd know the river is dry\n[03:45.21] That sends me down to the river tonight, ay-ay-ay\n[03:54.45] Down to the river\n[03:58.35] My baby and I\n[04:01.43] Oh-oh, down to the river we ride, ay-ay-ay\n[04:08.58]",
