        "dateAdded": "2026-06-09T16:16:03.570Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:08.84] Two black Cadillacs driving in a slow parade\n[00:13.45] \n[00:16.74] Headlights shining bright in the middle of the day\n[00:24.78] One is for his wife\n[00:28.14] The other for the woman who loved him at night\n[00:32.61] Two black Cadillacs meeting for the first time\n[00:39.77] And the preacher said he was a good man\n[00:43.72] And his brother said he was a good friend\n[00:47.62] But the women in the two black veils didn't bother to cry\n[00:53.84] (Bye bye, bye bye)\n[00:55.86] Yeah, they took turns laying a rose down\n[00:59.57] Threw a handful of dirt into the deep ground\n[01:03.29] He's not the only one who had a secret to hide\n[01:09.88] Bye bye, bye bye, bye bye\n[01:12.52] Two black Cadillacs\n[01:16.42] Two black Cadillacs\n[01:20.99] Two months ago, his wife called the number on his phone\n[01:28.38] Turns out he'd been lying to both of them for oh so long\n[01:36.30] They decided then, he'd never get away with doing this to them\n[01:44.70] Two black Cadillacs waiting for the right time, right time\n[01:52.16] And the preacher said he was a good man\n[01:55.33] And his brother said he was a good friend\n[01:59.56] But the women in the two black veils didn't bother to cry\n[02:05.23] (Bye bye, bye bye)\n[02:07.45] Yeah, they took turns laying a rose down\n[02:11.45] Threw a handful of dirt into the deep ground\n[02:15.88] He's not the only one who had a secret to hide\n[02:21.37] Bye bye, bye bye, bye bye\n[02:25.77] Yeah, yeah\n[02:28.88] (Two black Cadillacs)\n[02:32.56] It was the first and the last time they saw each other face to face\n[02:39.92] They shared a crimson smile and just walked away\n[02:47.21] And left the secret at the grave\n[02:51.85] And the preacher said he was a good man\n[02:55.74] And his brother said he was a good friend\n[02:59.28] But the women in the two black veils didn't bother to cry\n[03:05.46] (Bye bye, bye bye)\n[03:07.99] Yeah, they took turns laying a rose down\n[03:11.82] Threw a handful of dirt into the deep ground\n[03:16.38] He's not the only one who had a secret to hide\n[03:21.33] Bye bye, bye bye, bye bye\n[03:26.27] \n[03:30.38] Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah\n[03:33.59]",
