        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:13.268] I used to rule the world\n[00:17.018] Seas would rise when I gave the word\n[00:19.824] Now in the morning I sleep alone\n[00:23.920] Sweep the streets I used to own\n[00:41.121] I used to roll the dice\n[00:44.785] Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes\n[00:47.886] Listen as the crowd would sing\n[00:51.877] Now the old king is dead\n[00:53.697] Long live the king\n[00:54.913] One minute I held the key\n[00:58.793] Next the walls were closed on me\n[01:01.619] And I discovered that my castles stand\n[01:05.748] Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand\n[01:09.482] I hear Jerusalem bells are ringing\n[01:13.137] Roman Cavalry choirs are singing\n[01:16.633] Be my mirror my sword and shield\n[01:20.049] My missionaries in a foreign field\n[01:23.625] For some reason I can't explain\n[01:27.040] Once you go there was never\n[01:29.756] Never an honest word\n[01:33.755] But that was when I ruled the world\n[01:50.241] It was the wicked and wild wind\n[01:54.359] Blew down the doors to let me in\n[01:57.238] Shattered windows and the sound of drums\n[02:01.339] People couldn't believe what I'd become\n[02:04.674] Revolutionaries wait\n[02:08.442] For my head on a silver plate\n[02:11.391] Just a puppet on a lonely string\n[02:15.472] Oh who would ever want to be king\n[02:19.295] I hear Jerusalem bells are ringing\n[02:22.696] Roman Cavalry choirs are singing\n[02:26.161] Be my mirror my sword and shield\n[02:29.627] My missionaries in a foreign field\n[02:33.148] For some reason I can't explain\n[02:36.480] I know Saint Peter won't call my name\n[02:39.833] Never an honest word\n[02:43.230] But that was when I ruled the world\n[02:59.853] Oh oh oh oh oh oh\n[03:03.164] Oh oh oh oh oh oh\n[03:06.668] Oh oh oh oh oh oh\n[03:10.117] Oh oh oh oh oh oh\n[03:13.668] Oh oh oh oh oh\n[03:15.308] Hear Jerusalem bells are ringing\n[03:18.382] Roman Cavalry choirs are singing\n[03:21.810] Be my mirror my sword and shield\n[03:25.267] My missionaries in a foreign field\n[03:28.753] For some reason I can't explain\n[03:32.076] I know Saint Peter won't call my name\n[03:35.425] Never an honest word\n[03:38.656] But that was when I ruled the world",
