        "chorus": "",
        "chorusCue": "",
        "chorusTitle": "Block 2",
        "dateAdded": "2026-05-20T19:55:32.640Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:19.95] Headin' down south to the land of the pines\n[00:22.76] I'm thumbin' my way into North Caroline\n[00:25.66] Starin' up the road and pray to God I see headlights\n[00:32.49] I made it down the coast in seventeen hours\n[00:35.43] Pickin' me a bouquet of dogwood flowers\n[00:38.72] And I'm a-hopin' for Raleigh, I can see my baby tonight\n[00:44.63] So, rock me mama like a wagon wheel\n[00:48.28] Rock me mama any way you feel\n[00:51.83] Hey... mama rock me\n[00:58.51] Rock me mama like the wind and the rain\n[01:01.52] Rock me mama like a southbound train\n[01:04.73] Hey... mama rock me\n[01:10.31] \n[01:24.78] Runnin' from the cold up in New England\n[01:27.78] I was born to be a fiddler in an old time string band\n[01:31.06] My baby plays a guitar, I pick a banjo now\n[01:37.80] Oh, north country winters keep a-gettin' me down\n[01:40.44] Lost my money playin' poker, so I had to leave town\n[01:43.88] But I ain't a-turnin' back to livin' that old life no more\n[01:50.17] So, rock me mama like a wagon wheel\n[01:53.25] Rock me mama any way you feel\n[01:56.73] Hey... mama rock me\n[02:03.36] Yeah, rock me mama like the wind and the rain\n[02:06.15] Rock me mama like a southbound train\n[02:09.81] Hey... mama rock me\n[02:15.81] \n[02:42.46] Walkin' to the south out of Roanoke\n[02:45.68] I caught a trucker out of Philly, had a nice long toke\n[02:48.72] But he's a-headin' west from the Cumberland Gap\n[02:51.98] To Johnson City, Tennessee\n[02:55.06] And I gotta get a move on before the sun\n[02:58.21] I hear my baby callin' my name and I know that she's the only one\n[03:02.04] And if I died in Raleigh, at least I will die free\n[03:08.01] So, rock me mama like a wagon wheel\n[03:11.38] Rock me mama any way you feel\n[03:14.60] Hey... mama rock me\n[03:20.10] Oh, rock me mama like the wind and the rain\n[03:24.30] Rock me mama like a southbound train\n[03:27.72] Hey... mama rock me\n[03:34.03] So, rock me mama like a wagon wheel\n[03:37.18] Rock me mama any way you feel (oh, I wanna feel)\n[03:40.95] Hey... mama rock me\n[03:47.04] Rock me mama like the wind and the rain\n[03:50.31] Rock me mama like a southbound train\n[03:53.89] Hey... mama rock me\n[03:58.47]",
