        "dateAdded": "2026-06-09T15:46:50.372Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:14.72] She grew up watching hockey\n[00:17.74] With her daddy on Saturday nights\n[00:21.78] He taught her how to tie her skates\n[00:25.35] Her brothers taught her how to fight\n[00:28.03] She can wear high heels or flannel\n[00:31.33] She can look sexy in a toque\n[00:35.19] She likes snow storms and Gordon Lightfoot\n[00:38.75] And if you're lucky she'll love you\n[00:41.65] Canadian girls, Canadian girls\n[00:48.67] Irresistible, lovable, trouble though sometimes girls\n[00:55.42] We could travel the world\n[00:59.21] From New York to Paris, France\n[01:03.31] But we're always gonna come back Canadian girls\n[01:10.64] My baby she likes to snowboard\n[01:13.06] And spend her summers out on a boat\n[01:16.92] Thinks the perfect night out is a cabin\n[01:19.92] Smell of coffee on an old wood-stove\n[01:23.43] She won't admit, but she watched Degrassi\n[01:27.51] She's proud and sometimes quiet\n[01:31.27] A true north national treasure.\n[01:34.12] She'd give her life for the red and white\n[01:37.23] Canadian girls, Canadian girls\n[01:44.03] Irresistible, lovable, trouble though sometimes girls\n[01:50.38] We could travel the world\n[01:55.35] From New York to Paris, France\n[01:58.79] But we're always gonna come back Canadian girls\n[02:21.74] Well us boys we like our fishin'\n[02:26.09] Our Hockey and Ron McLean\n[02:29.77] We like Moosehead beer and whitetail deer\n[02:33.58] Stomping Tom and the UFC\n[02:36.78] And we like the foreign ladies\n[02:40.30] Their accents are really nice\n[02:43.83] But there ain't nothin like our northern girls\n[02:47.67] To keep us warm at night\n[02:50.26] Canadian girls, Canadian girls\n[02:57.66] Irresistible, lovable, trouble though sometimes girls\n[03:03.31] We could travel the world\n[03:08.54] From New York to Paris, France\n[03:12.02] But we're always gonna come back Canadian girls\n[03:18.87] From Tuktoyaktuk to Newfoundland\n[03:26.01] You keep us coming back Canadian girls\n[03:40.45]",
