        "fullLyrics": "[00:11.98] A gang of kids on their peddle bikes\n[00:14.85] In a dusty town, way to ride\n[00:17.59] To the general store for popeye cigarettes\n[00:23.22] Class of '99\n[00:25.68] Yeah we lived, laughed, loved and cried\n[00:28.13] Took for granted that those days would never end\n[00:33.98] Living like that yearbook picture wouldn't fade\n[00:39.05] And some standing right beside me, I might never see again\n[00:44.13] The trouble is\n[00:46.27] You think you have time\n[00:49.67] You think tomorrows always coming down the line\n[00:54.95] And then one day\n[00:57.36] You wake up and you find\n[01:00.36] The trouble is you thought you had time\n[01:08.25] Student hire and a fancy job\n[01:11.57] Big old house, two car garage\n[01:14.02] He works hard for his wife and his son\n[01:19.09] An empty seat at t-ball games\n[01:21.83] Just a sacrifice he'll make\n[01:24.85] Make it up, next weekend comes along\n[01:30.64] Years go by and that day comes too soon\n[01:35.68] That boy goes off to college, he stands in his empty room\n[01:40.73] The trouble is\n[01:43.02] You think you have time\n[01:45.94] You think tomorrows always coming down the line\n[01:51.40] And then one day\n[01:54.18] You wake up and you find\n[01:57.07] The trouble is you thought you had time\n[02:01.90] \n[02:15.82] Shotgun shells and a tackle box\n[02:18.83] On the floorboard of a truck\n[02:21.43] Morning sun burning fog off a lake\n[02:26.81] A teenage girl and her grandad\n[02:29.39] He takes her fishing but he feels bad\n[02:32.31] She can't take her eyes off that Facebook page\n[02:37.64] But someday soon, who knows how long\n[02:42.77] She'll look up from that phone and he'll be gone\n[02:48.15] The trouble is\n[02:50.62] You think you have time\n[02:53.52] You think tomorrows always coming down the line\n[02:58.68] And then one day\n[03:01.59] You wake up and you find\n[03:04.30] The trouble is you thought you had time\n[03:09.83] The trouble is you thought you had time\n[03:15.07]",
