        "dateAdded": "2026-06-05T17:27:15.845Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[01:07.20] These mist-covered mountains\n[01:13.51] Are a home now for me\n[01:17.64] \n[01:19.82] But my home is in lowlands\n[01:26.62] And always will be\n[01:30.06] \n[01:32.20] Someday, you'll return to\n[01:38.69] Your valleys and your farms\n[01:44.96] And you'll no longer burn\n[01:47.46] To be brothers in arms\n[01:53.00] \n[02:09.64] Through these fields of destruction\n[02:16.21] Baptisms of fire\n[02:20.07] \n[02:22.47] I've witnessed your suffering\n[02:28.51] As the battle raged higher\n[02:32.55] \n[02:34.62] And though they did hurt me so bad\n[02:40.64] In the fear and alarm\n[02:44.71] \n[02:46.74] You did not desert me\n[02:49.71] My brothers in arms\n[02:54.65] \n[03:10.25] There's so many different worlds\n[03:16.88] So many different suns\n[03:23.13] And we have just one world\n[03:29.16] But we live in different ones\n[03:33.77] \n[04:05.35] Now the sun's gone to hell, and\n[04:12.09] The moon's riding high\n[04:17.42] Let me bid you farewell\n[04:21.70] \n[04:24.07] Every man has to die\n[04:27.78] \n[04:30.17] But it's written in the starlight\n[04:36.06] And every line in your palm\n[04:41.86] We're fools to make war\n[04:44.70] On our brothers in arms\n[04:47.37]",
