        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[01:08.03] Sweet surrender on the quayside\n[01:15.47] You remember we used to run and hide\n[01:21.66] In the shadow of the cargoes I take you one time\n[01:25.35] And we're counting all the numbers down to the waterline\n[01:31.73] Well, near misses on the dogleap stairways\n[01:39.85] French kisses in the darkened doorways\n[01:46.14] A foghorn blowing out a wild and cold\n[01:49.80] A policeman shines a light on my shoulder\n[01:54.57] \n[02:10.67] Up comes a coaster, fast and silent in the night\n[02:17.68] Over my shoulder all you can see are the pilot lights\n[02:24.31] No money in our jackets and our jeans are torn\n[02:27.88] Your hands are cold but your lips are warm\n[02:45.56] \n[03:12.35] She can see him on the jetty where they used to know\n[03:19.31] She can feel him in the places where the sailors go\n[03:26.33] When she's walking by the river or the railway line\n[03:29.71] She can still hear him whisper:\n[03:31.97] \"Let's go down to the waterline\"\n[03:36.09] Come on\n[03:38.29]",
        "genre": [
            "Rock"
        ],
