        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:41.95] Getting crazy on the waltzers\n[00:45.21] But it's the life that I choose\n[00:47.30] \n[00:49.44] Hey, sing about the six blade, sing about the switchback\n[00:53.94] And a torture tattoo\n[00:55.66] And I've been riding on a ghost train\n[00:59.19] Where the cars, they scream and slam\n[01:02.99] And I don't know where I'll be tonight\n[01:07.00] But I'd always tell you where I am\n[01:09.80] In a screaming ring of faces\n[01:12.86] I seen her standing in the light\n[01:16.55] She had a ticket for the races\n[01:19.20] Yeah, just like me, she was a victim of the night\n[01:23.50] I put my hand upon the lever\n[01:26.63] Said let it rock and let it roll\n[01:30.41] I had the one-arm bandit fever\n[01:34.46] There was an arrow through my heart and my soul\n[01:37.69] And the big wheel keep on turnin'\n[01:41.38] Neon burnin' up above\n[01:45.39] And I'm just high on the world\n[01:48.44] Come on and take a low ride with me girl\n[01:52.40] On the tunnel of love\n[01:55.11] Yeah, love\n[01:57.65] \n[01:59.69] It's just a danger\n[02:01.92] When you're riding at your own risk\n[02:05.32] She said, \"You are the perfect stranger\"\n[02:09.30] She said, \"Baby, let's keep it like this\"\n[02:13.13] It's just a cakewalk, twisting baby, yeah, step right up and say\n[02:20.55] \"Hey mister, give me two, give me two now\n[02:24.00] 'Cause any two can play\"\n[02:26.32] And the big wheel keep on turning\n[02:30.42] Neon burnin' up above\n[02:34.05] And I'm just high on the world\n[02:37.22] Come on and take a low ride with me, girl\n[02:41.56] On the tunnel of love\n[02:44.00] Oh love, love\n[02:48.29] Well it's been money for muscle on a another whirligig\n[02:52.75] Money for muscle and another girl I dig\n[02:56.38] Another hustle just to\n[02:58.09] Just to make it big and rock away, rock away\n[03:02.66] Oh rock away, rock away\n[03:06.25] And girl, it looks so pretty to me\n[03:09.55] Like it always did\n[03:12.94] Oh, like the Spanish city to me\n[03:16.44] When we were kids\n[03:19.88] Yeah, girl it looks so pretty to me\n[03:23.24] Just like it always did\n[03:26.81] Oh, like the Spanish city to me\n[03:30.48] When we were kids\n[03:33.08] \n[03:35.63] Woh la!\n[03:37.92] \n[03:45.63] Check it out\n[03:47.71] \n[04:07.14] She took off her silver locket\n[04:10.26] She said, \"Remember me by this\"\n[04:13.88] She put her hand in my pocket\n[04:17.69] I got a keepsake and a kiss\n[04:20.99] And in the roar of dust and diesel\n[04:24.22] I stood and watched her walk away\n[04:26.37] \n[04:29.43] I could have caught up with her easy enough\n[04:32.58] But something must have made me stay\n[04:34.88] And the big wheel keep on turning\n[04:38.50] Neon burnin' up above\n[04:42.40] And I'm just high on this world\n[04:45.26] Come on and take a low ride with me, girl\n[04:49.74] On the tunnel of love\n[04:52.36] Yea love, love\n[04:56.63] On the tunnel of love\n[04:59.36] Woah love, love\n[05:03.15] Yeah, now I'm searchin' through these carousels and the carnival arcades\n[05:07.09] Searching everywhere from steeplechase to palisades\n[05:10.78] In any shooting gallery where promises are made\n[05:14.07] To rock away, rock away\n[05:17.58] Rock away, rock away\n[05:21.46] From Cullercoats to Whitley bay\n[05:24.32] And to rock away\n[05:28.71] And, girl it looks so pretty to me\n[05:32.45] Like it always did\n[05:36.25] Like the Spanish city to me\n[05:41.18] When we were kids\n[05:43.66] Girl, it looks so pretty to me\n[05:48.10] Like it always did\n[05:50.52] Like the Spanish city to me\n[05:54.28] When we were kids\n[05:55.66]",
