        "fullLyrics": "[00:30.28] Things were all good yesterday\n[00:32.68] And then the devil took your memory\n[00:35.20] And if you fell to your death today\n[00:37.63] I hope that heaven is your resting place\n[00:40.17] I heard the doctors put your chest in pain\n[00:42.46] But then that could've been the medicine\n[00:44.96] And now you're lying in the bed again\n[00:47.11] Either way, I'll cry with the rest of them\n[00:49.84] And my father told me, \"Son\n[00:53.12] It's not his fault he doesn't know your face\n[00:59.17] And you're not the only one\"\n[01:02.81] Although my grandma used to say\n[01:07.05] That he used to sing\n[01:09.08] Darling, hold me in your arms the way you did last night\n[01:13.83] And we'll lie inside for a little while here, oh\n[01:19.00] I could look into your eyes until the sun comes up\n[01:23.45] And we're wrapped in light and life and love\n[01:28.86] Put your open lips on mine and slowly let them shut\n[01:33.51] For they're designed to be together, oh\n[01:38.48] With your body next to mine, our hearts will beat as one\n[01:43.27] And we're set alight, we're afire love\n[01:49.59] Love, love\n[01:54.81] \n[01:58.41] And things were all good yesterday\n[02:01.00] But then the devil took your breath away\n[02:03.52] And now we're left here in the pain\n[02:05.49] Black suit, black tie, standing in the rain\n[02:08.16] And now my family is one again\n[02:09.92] Stapled together with the strangers and a friend\n[02:12.63] Came to my mind, I should paint it with a pen\n[02:15.15] Six years old, I remember when\n[02:18.00] My father told me, \"Son\n[02:21.41] It's not his fault he doesn't know your face\n[02:27.74] And you're not the only one\"\n[02:31.11] Although my grandma used to say\n[02:34.94] That he used to sing\n[02:37.43] Darling, hold me in your arms the way you did last night\n[02:42.07] And we'll lie inside for a little while here, oh\n[02:47.11] I could look into your eyes until the sun comes up\n[02:51.83] And we're wrapped in light and life and love\n[02:57.02] Put your open lips on mine and slowly let them shut\n[03:01.73] For they're designed to be together, oh\n[03:06.41] With your body next to mine, our hearts will beat as one\n[03:11.24] And we're set alight, we're afire love\n[03:17.28] Love, love\n[03:21.70] See the love, the love, the love, the love\n[03:26.08] See the love, the love, the love, the love\n[03:31.18] See the love, the love, the love, the love\n[03:34.85] And my father and all of my family\n[03:39.04] Rise from their seats to sing hallelujah\n[03:44.19] And my mother and all of my family\n[03:48.94] Rise from their seats to sing hallelujah\n[03:54.11] And my brother and all of my family\n[03:58.69] Rise from their seats to sing hallelujah\n[04:03.45] (And all my brothers and my sisters, yeah, ah)\n[04:05.32] And my father and all of my family\n[04:08.62] Rise from their seats to sing hallelujah\n[04:13.76] \n[04:20.34] To the love, the love, the love, the love\n[04:25.38] To the love, the love, the love, the love\n[04:30.14] To the love, the love, the love, the love\n[04:32.62]",
