        "dateAdded": "2026-05-20T14:32:57.397Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:28.03] Well the key to my survival\n[00:32.98] Was never in much doubt\n[00:37.57] The question was, how I could keep sane\n[00:42.55] Trying to find a way out?\n[00:47.56] Things were never easy for me\n[00:51.26] Peace of mind was hard to find\n[00:55.95] And I needed a place where I could hide\n[01:00.96] Somewhere I could call mine\n[01:05.62] I didn't think much about it\n[01:09.59] 'Til it started happening all the time\n[01:14.73] Soon I was living with the fear everyday\n[01:19.25] Of what might happen that night\n[01:24.14] I couldn't stand to hear the crying\n[01:28.08] Of my mother, and I remember when\n[01:32.33] I swore that that would be the last they'd see of me\n[01:37.42] And I never went home again\n[01:42.74] They say that time is a healer\n[01:46.20] And now my wounds are not the same\n[01:52.08] I rang the bell with my heart in my mouth\n[01:56.07] I had to hear what he'd say\n[02:01.22] He sat me down to talk to me\n[02:05.73] He looked me straight in the eyes\n[02:09.33] He said\n[02:11.11] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[02:15.59] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[02:20.12] \"You walked out, you left us behind\"\n[02:24.63] \"And you're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[02:29.62] \n[02:33.77] Oh, his words how they hurt me, I'll never forget it\n[02:39.91] \n[02:42.65] And as the time, it went by, I lived to regret it\n[02:47.92] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[02:52.62] But where should I go and what should I do?\n[02:57.18] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[03:01.79] But I came here for help, oh I came here for you\n[03:07.93] \n[03:23.40] Well the years they passed so slowly\n[03:28.43] I thought about him everyday\n[03:33.26] What would I do, if we passed on the street\n[03:38.06] Would I keep running away?\n[03:42.69] In and out of hiding places\n[03:47.12] Soon I'd have to face the facts\n[03:51.48] We'd have to sit down and talk it over\n[03:56.38] And that would mean going back\n[04:01.26] They say that time is a healer\n[04:04.83] And now my wounds are not the same\n[04:10.23] But I rang that bell with my heart in my mouth\n[04:14.54] I had to hear what he'd say\n[04:19.67] He sat me down to talk to me\n[04:24.35] He looked me straight in the eyes\n[04:27.79] He said\n[04:29.38] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[04:33.93] \"You're no son, no son of mine\"\n[04:38.56] \"When you walked out, you left us behind\"\n[04:43.00] \"And you're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[04:47.97] \n[04:52.37] Oh, his words how they hurt me\n[04:54.98] I'll never forget it\n[04:58.17] \n[05:01.01] And as the time, it went by\n[05:04.07] I lived to regret it\n[05:06.20] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[05:11.06] But where should I go and what should I do?\n[05:15.44] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[05:20.26] Well I came here for help, oh I was looking for you\n[05:24.78] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine oh\"\n[05:30.87] \"You're no son\" ha yeah, ha yeah, ha yeah, ha yeah, ha yeah\n[05:39.14] \"You're no son, you're no son of mine\"\n[05:44.07] Oh, oh\n[05:46.47] Oh, oh\n[05:48.78] Oh, oh\n[05:51.13] Oh, oh\n[05:53.23] Oh, oh\n[05:55.68] Oh, oh\n[05:57.96] Oh, oh\n[05:59.82] You're no son of mine (oh, oh)\n[06:02.77] (Oh, oh) You're no son of mine (oh, oh)\n[06:06.32] You're no son (oh, oh), you're no son of mine (oh, oh)\n[06:11.96] Oh, oh\n[06:14.10] Oh, oh\n[06:16.47] Oh, oh\n[06:17.83] You're no son of mine (oh, oh)\n[06:21.06] Oh, oh\n[06:23.56] Oh, oh\n[06:25.61] Oh, oh\n[06:28.09] Oh, oh\n[06:30.33] Oh, oh\n[06:32.72] Oh, oh\n[06:34.97] Oh, oh\n[06:35.82]",
