        "fullLyrics": "[00:16.49] Yeah, I'm chillin' on a dirt road\n[00:19.68] Laid back swervin' like I'm George Jones\n[00:23.13] Smoke rollin' out the window\n[00:26.82] An ice-cold beer sittin' in the console\n[00:30.39] Memory lane up in the headlights\n[00:34.08] It's got me reminiscing on them good times\n[00:37.70] I'm turnin' off a real life drive and that's right\n[00:42.51] I'm hittin' easy street on mud tires\n[00:45.57] Back in the day, Pott's farm was the place to go\n[00:48.73] Load the truck up, hit the dirt road\n[00:50.37] Jump the barbed wire, spread the word\n[00:52.42] Light the bonfire, then call the girls\n[00:54.05] The king in the can and the Marlboro man\n[00:55.96] Jack'n'Jim were a few good men\n[00:58.08] Where ya learned how to kiss and cuss and fight too\n[00:59.97] Better watch out for the boys in blue\n[01:01.56] And all this small town he said, she said\n[01:03.67] Ain't it funny how rumors spread\n[01:05.76] Like I know something y'all don't know\n[01:07.32] Man that talk is gettin' old\n[01:09.22] Ya better mind your business, man, watch your mouth\n[01:11.15] Before I have to knock that loud mouth out\n[01:13.04] I'm tired of talkin', man, y'all ain't listenin'\n[01:14.89] Them old dirt roads is what y'all missin'\n[01:16.75] I'm chillin' on a dirt road\n[01:20.29] Laid back swervin' like I'm George Jones\n[01:23.92] Smoke rollin' out the window\n[01:27.18] An ice-cold beer sittin' in the console\n[01:31.43] Memory lane up in the headlights\n[01:34.68] It's got me reminiscing on them good times\n[01:38.65] I'm turnin' off a real life drive and that's right\n[01:42.84] I'm hittin' easy street on mud tires\n[01:46.08] I sit back and think about them good old days\n[01:49.07] The way we were raised, and our southern ways\n[01:50.76] And we like cornbread, and biscuits\n[01:52.57] And if it's broke round here we fix it\n[01:54.77] I can take y'all where ya need to go\n[01:56.56] Down to my hood, back in them woods\n[01:58.46] We do it different around here, that's right\n[02:00.53] But we sure do it good, and we do it all night\n[02:02.20] See, if you really wanna know how it feels\n[02:04.34] To get off the road with trucks and four wheels\n[02:06.16] Jump on in, and man, tell your friends\n[02:07.75] We'll raise some hell where the black top ends\n[02:09.68] I'm chillin' on a dirt road\n[02:13.14] Laid back swervin' like I'm George Jones\n[02:16.33] Smoke rollin' out the window\n[02:19.84] An ice-cold beer sittin' in the console\n[02:23.80] Memory lane up in the headlights\n[02:27.59] It's got me reminiscing on them good times\n[02:31.28] I'm turnin' off a real life drive and that's right\n[02:35.53] I'm hittin' easy street on mud tires\n[02:38.44] That's right\n[02:41.01] \n[02:46.53] Yeah, I'm chillin' on a dirt road\n[02:50.95] \n[02:58.51] Laid back swervin' like I'm George Jones\n[03:02.59] Smoke rollin' out the window\n[03:05.41] An ice-cold beer sittin' in the console\n[03:09.43] Memory lane up in the headlights\n[03:12.98] It's got me reminiscing on them good times\n[03:17.45] I'm turning off of real life, drivin' that's right\n[03:21.23] I'm hittin' easy street on mud tires\n[03:24.12] That's right\n[03:26.68]",
