        "fullLyrics": "[00:14.26] Well, I heard there was a secret chord\n[00:18.06] That David played, and it pleased the Lord\n[00:21.43] But you don't really care for music, do ya?\n[00:28.14] Well, it goes like this: the fourth, the fifth\n[00:32.00] The minor fall and the major lift\n[00:35.38] The baffled king composing Hallelujah\n[00:42.05] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[00:49.19] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[01:04.13] Well, baby, I've been here before\n[01:07.58] I've seen this room, and I've walked this floor\n[01:10.31] You know, I used to live alone before I knew ya\n[01:17.86] And I've seen your flag on the marble arch\n[01:21.55] And love is not a victory march\n[01:24.86] It's a cold and it's a broken Hallelujah\n[01:31.52] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[01:38.95] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[01:53.83] Well, there was a time when you let me know\n[01:57.42] What's really going on below\n[02:00.84] But now you never show that to me, do ya?\n[02:07.80] But remember when I moved in, you\n[02:11.61] And the holy dove was moving too\n[02:15.01] And every breath we drew was Hallelujah\n[02:21.13] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[02:28.13] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[02:37.44] \n[03:03.49] Well, maybe there is a God above\n[03:07.68] But all I've ever learned from love\n[03:10.87] Was how to shoot somebody who outdrew ya\n[03:19.65] And it's not a cry that you hear at night\n[03:23.50] It's not somebody who's seen the light\n[03:26.73] It's a cold, and it's a broken Hallelujah\n[03:33.04] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[03:40.26] Hallelujah, Hallelu-\n[03:47.69] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[03:54.58] Hallelujah, Hallelujah\n[04:09.90]",
