        "dateAdded": "2026-04-21T18:58:40.647Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:06.10] Almost heaven, West Virginia\n[00:11.68] Blue Ridge Mountains, Shenandoah River\n[00:18.88] Life is old there, older than the trees\n[00:23.75] Younger than the mountains, growin' like a breeze\n[00:28.74] Country roads, take me home\n[00:34.50] To the place I belong\n[00:40.14] West Virginia, Mountain Mama\n[00:45.81] Take me home, country roads\n[00:52.99] All my memories gather 'round her\n[00:58.65] Miner's lady, stranger to blue water\n[01:05.62] Dark and dusty, painted on the sky\n[01:10.52] Misty taste of moonshine, teardrops in my eyes\n[01:15.44] Country roads, take me home\n[01:21.09] To the place I belong\n[01:26.84] West Virginia, Mountain Mama\n[01:32.68] Take me home, country roads\n[01:39.34] I hear her voice, in the mornin' hour she calls me\n[01:44.84] Radio reminds me of my home far away\n[01:50.59] Driving down the road, I get a feeling\n[01:54.19] That I should have been home yesterday, yesterday\n[02:01.35] Country roads, take me home\n[02:07.14] To the place I belong\n[02:12.71] West Virginia, Mountain Mama\n[02:18.53] Take me home, country roads\n[02:22.56] Everybody sing it\n[02:24.15] Country roads, take me home\n[02:29.86] To the place I belong\n[02:35.50] West Virginia, Mountain Mama\n[02:41.16] Take me home, country roads\n[02:46.80] Take me home down country roads\n[02:52.59] Take me home down country roads\n[02:56.79]",
