        "fullLyrics": "[00:13.88] Well, she was precious like a flower\n[00:18.84] And she grew wild, wild but innocent\n[00:27.22] A perfect prayer in a desperate hour\n[00:32.32] She was everything beautiful and different\n[00:38.58] Stupid boy, you can't fence that in\n[00:45.27] Stupid boy, it's like holdin' back the wind\n[00:52.24] She laid her heart and soul right in your hands\n[00:58.96] And you stole her every dream, and you crushed her plans\n[01:05.35] She never even knew she had a choice, and that's what happens\n[01:10.64] When the only voice she hears is telling her she can't\n[01:18.30] Stupid boy, stupid boy, oh\n[01:31.46] So, what made you think you could take a life\n[01:38.31] And just push it, push it around?\n[01:45.67] I guess to build yourself up so high\n[01:50.73] You had to take her and break her down, oh\n[01:57.98] Well, she laid her heart and soul right in your hands\n[02:04.81] And you stole her every dream, and you crushed her plans\n[02:11.24] She never even knew she had a choice, and that's what happens\n[02:16.63] When the only voice she hears is telling her she can't\n[02:23.61] You stupid boy, oh, you always had to be right\n[02:31.16] But now you lost the only thing\n[02:33.37] That ever made you feel alive\n[02:38.13] \n[02:40.76] Oh, oh\n[02:44.02] Ooh, ooh\n[02:47.67] Yeah, yeah\n[02:50.72] Well, she laid her heart and soul right in your hands, yeah\n[02:57.29] And you stole her every dream, and you crushed her plans\n[03:02.94] Yes, you did\n[03:03.92] She never even knew she had a choice, and that's what happens\n[03:09.17] When the only voice she hears is telling her she can't\n[03:16.39] You stupid boy\n[03:19.70] Oh, I'm the same old, same old stupid boy\n[03:31.31] It took a while for her to figure out\n[03:34.72] She could run, but when she did\n[03:38.22] She was long gone, long gone\n[03:51.31] \n[04:15.40] Ooh, oh, she was gone\n[04:22.59] She's long gone\n[04:28.46] Mm, yeah, she is now\n[04:38.17] Yeah, oh\n[04:43.34] \n[05:08.24] Oh, no one's ever gonna love me like she loved me\n[05:14.71] And she loved me, she loved me\n[05:16.78] God, please, just let her know\n[05:19.61] I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, baby\n[05:29.12] Yeah, I'm down on my knees\n[05:33.94] She's never coming back to me\n[05:42.44]",
