        "fullLyrics": "[00:14.74] We were just a couple years short of the age\n[00:17.81] By my name on a fake ID\n[00:20.39] And still 'bout a hundred away from the day\n[00:23.95] Your daddy said you could run with me\n[00:26.32] We were a couple of line steppers\n[00:29.32] Who just couldn't wait to step over the line\n[00:32.44] Never thinkin' we wouldn't last\n[00:35.58] I was your first and you were mine\n[00:38.54] We were leather jackets hangin' onto a Harley\n[00:41.78] Two heartbeats in the moonlight\n[00:44.64] We were feet hangin' out over the edge of the water tower skyline\n[00:49.94] At least there's a little bit of sweet in the bitter\n[00:54.09] Though a part of me is always gonna miss her\n[00:56.79] I am who I am, I just miss who I was when we were\n[01:04.91] \n[01:08.45] Um-hm\n[01:11.83] \n[01:14.04] We were gonna make it work weren't we, baby?\n[01:17.61] Had it all laid out in our mind\n[01:19.84] By the time we knew time was runnin' out\n[01:23.06] We done run out of time\n[01:25.25] And we were downtown Saturday night, last-call cover band\n[01:30.95] 'Til the last song played, never thought we'd fade\n[01:34.70] Like the stamp on the back of her hand\n[01:37.36] We were her on my shoulders, lighter in the air\n[01:40.80] \"Pour Some Sugar On Me\"\n[01:43.49] We were top down at Johnson's field\n[01:46.66] When she whispered that she wants me\n[01:49.38] At least there's a little bit of sweet in the bitter\n[01:53.07] Though a part of me is always gonna miss her\n[01:55.42] I am who I am, I just miss who I was when we were\n[02:03.12] Um-hm\n[02:06.07] \n[02:13.67] We were leather jackets hangin' onto a Harley\n[02:16.96] Two heartbeats in the moonlight\n[02:19.15] We were feet hangin' out over the edge of the water tower skyline\n[02:23.86] At least there's a little bit of sweet in the bitter\n[02:28.81] Though a part of me is always gonna miss her\n[02:31.46] I am who I am, I just miss who I was when we were\n[02:38.98] Mhm, yes I do\n[02:43.13] \n[02:45.96] Friends say\n[02:49.95] Oh well, let that ship sail\n[02:52.23] You gotta let go of her\n[02:54.84] Just wasn't meant to be\n[02:56.80] But somewhere down deep I still believe\n[03:00.58] That we were\n[03:01.96]",
