        "fullLyrics": "[00:18.25] I heard a song 'bout a ramblin' man\n[00:22.81] Bought a guitar and I started a band\n[00:27.17] I got a gig at the local Am Vet\n[00:30.91] And I was gone and I ain't back yet\n[00:36.03] \n[00:45.06] '69 bored, out and jacked up\n[00:49.68] A quarter mile that was all it was\n[00:54.19] I burned the cool off of that Corvette\n[00:57.77] And I was gone and I ain't back yet\n[01:03.40] Lookin' back at the moments, black and white\n[01:08.44] I wouldn't change a thing that changed my life\n[01:13.61] For the worse, for the better\n[01:17.51] Man, I was gone, gone forever\n[01:30.48] She was a cut offs pepper sauce queen\n[01:34.50] Man, we were matches and gasoline\n[01:39.05] First taste of love never will forget\n[01:42.65] I was gone and I ain't back yet\n[01:47.35] I was gone, gone and I ain't back yet\n[01:52.95] Lookin' back at the moments, black white\n[01:57.98] I wouldn't change a thing that changed my life\n[02:02.92] For the worse, for the better\n[02:06.92] Man, I was gone, gone forever\n[02:19.83] The laughs, the smiles, the trials, the tears\n[02:24.19] It's hard to hate what got me here\n[02:31.53] What got me here\n[02:37.50] She was a straight out of Hollywood smile\n[02:41.93] We missed it all by a country mile\n[02:46.53] Went out one night for some cigarettes\n[02:50.08] And I was gone and I ain't back yet\n[02:54.67] I was gone, gone and I ain't back yet\n[02:58.75] I was gone and I ain't back\n[03:03.69] Ain't back, ain't back yet\n[03:07.83] And I was gone and I ain't back yet\n[03:12.77] I was gone and I ain't back yet\n[03:17.06] I was gone, gone and I ain't back yet\n[03:22.85] (Gone, ain't back yet)\n[03:27.13] (Gone, ain't back yet)\n[03:31.66] (Gone, ain't back yet)\n[03:36.14] (Gone, ain't back yet)\n[03:40.51] (Gone, ain't back yet)\n[03:46.87] (Ain't back yet)\n[03:50.37]",
