        "fullLyrics": "[00:10.06] There's a trail of smoke comin' out of a bottle\n[00:14.98] If you look real close, you can see it right there\n[00:19.74] A little tin roof bar down a path you have to follow\n[00:23.92] From a treasure map with the edges burnt\n[00:26.32] From a few too many beers\n[00:29.38] We'll pull the ropes off the boat\n[00:31.87] We'll throw 'em up on the dock\n[00:34.15] We'll let the stars be our guide\n[00:36.77] No, we don't need no clock\n[00:38.66] We'll set sail\n[00:42.04] Yeah, I'll see you there\n[00:43.30] Waving your hair with that t-shirt on\n[00:45.96] Dead men tell no tales\n[00:47.91] It's like nowhere else you've ever been\n[00:52.67] We'll write your name on a dollar bill\n[00:55.43] Put it on a wall, it'll still be there\n[00:57.98] Next time we come back, girl\n[01:00.41] To the bar at the end of the world\n[01:04.60] \n[01:12.44] In that old seashell, you can hear the ocean\n[01:17.42] You can hear the waves crash and whisper in your ear\n[01:22.21] Little glow in the night, it's the last place open\n[01:26.36] And the house drink is a beautiful thing called \"Make me disappear\"\n[01:31.76] We'll throw the ropes off the boat\n[01:34.45] We'll throw 'em up on the dock\n[01:36.61] We'll let the stars be our guide\n[01:39.07] No, we don't need no clock\n[01:40.92] We'll set sail\n[01:44.20] Yeah, I'll see you there\n[01:45.74] Waving your hair with that t-shirt on\n[01:48.33] Dead men tell no tales\n[01:50.27] It's like nowhere else you've ever been\n[01:55.19] We'll write your name on a dollar bill\n[01:57.70] Put it on a wall, it'll still be there\n[02:00.41] Next time we come back, girl\n[02:02.92] To the bar at the end of the world\n[02:08.94] \n[02:15.12] There ain't no empty glasses\n[02:17.30] They're playing \"Drift Away\"\n[02:19.69] That's where the magic happens\n[02:22.06] Back up in that little bay\n[02:24.26] We'll set sail\n[02:27.45] Yeah, I'll see you there\n[02:29.02] Waving your hair with that t-shirt on\n[02:31.47] Dead men tell no tales\n[02:33.51] It's like nowhere else you've ever been\n[02:38.52] We'll write your name on a dollar bill\n[02:41.04] Put it on a wall, it'll still be there\n[02:43.54] Next time we come back, girl\n[02:46.11] To the bar at the end of the world\n[02:50.85] To the bar at the end of the world\n[02:53.59] (We'll set sail)\n[02:55.74] \n[03:01.43] End of the world\n[03:03.06] (We'll set sail)\n[03:03.21]",
