        "dateAdded": "2026-05-01T05:52:41.211Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:21.26] Jack and Diane painted a picture of my life and my dreams\n[00:26.34] Suddenly this crazy world made more sense to me\n[00:31.61] Well, I heard it today, and I couldn't help but sing along\n[00:36.67] 'Cause every time I hear that song\n[00:41.62] An' I go back to a two toned short bed Chevy\n[00:45.13] Drivin' my first love out to the levy\n[00:47.74] Livin' life with no sense of time\n[00:52.34] An' I go back to the feel of a 50-yard line\n[00:55.71] A blanket, a girl, some raspberry wine\n[00:58.05] Wishin' time would stop right in its tracks\n[01:03.88] Every time I hear that song\n[01:08.13] I'll go back, I'll go back\n[01:15.03] \n[01:17.19] \n[01:19.86] I used to rock all night long to, \"Keep On Rockin' Me Baby\"\n[01:24.26] Frat parties, college bars, just tryin' to impress the ladies\n[01:30.50] Well, I heard it today, and I couldn't help but sing along\n[01:35.23] 'Cause every time I hear that song\n[01:40.46] An' I go back to the smell of an old gym floor\n[01:43.68] The taste of salt on the Carolina shore\n[01:46.16] After graduation and drinkin' goodbye to friends\n[01:51.07] And I go back to watchin' summer fade to fall\n[01:54.10] Growin' up too fast and I do recall\n[01:56.68] Wishin' time would stop right in its tracks\n[02:01.83] Every time I hear that song\n[02:06.81] I'll go back, I'll go back\n[02:15.52] \n[02:19.07] We all have a song that somehow stamped our lives\n[02:23.75] Takes us to another place and time\n[02:29.10] \n[02:32.72] So I go back to a pew, preacher, and a choir\n[02:35.30] Singin' 'bout God, brimstone, and fire\n[02:37.96] And the smell of Sunday chicken after church\n[02:42.82] And I go back to the loss of a real good friend\n[02:45.98] And the 16 summers I shared with him\n[02:48.62] Now \"Only The Good Die Young\" stops me in my tracks\n[02:54.56] Every time I hear that song\n[02:58.58] I'll go back, I'll go back\n[03:07.37] \n[03:10.39] To the feel of a 50-yard line\n[03:12.97] A blanket, a girl, some raspberry wine\n[03:17.21] I'll go back (I'll go back)\n[03:21.03] To watchin' summer fade to fall\n[03:23.22] Growin' up too fast and I do recall\n[03:27.61] I'll go back (I'll go back)\n[03:32.18] To the loss of a real good friend\n[03:33.90] And the sixteen summers I shared with him\n[03:38.45] I'll go back\n[03:41.06] I'll go back, I'll go back\n[03:47.94]",
        "genre": [
            "Country",
            "Rock"
        ],
