        "fullLyrics": "[00:29.01] Saw him sittin' on a side walk in Fresno\n[00:31.27] Braided hair and a tie-dyed t-shirt on\n[00:35.61] Talkin' to himself about Vietnam\n[00:38.76] 'Bout the tour he did and the deal he got\n[00:42.38] He said, \"This world ain't the same if you ask me\"\n[00:46.39] If I could be somewhere else, I'd tell you where I'd be.\n[00:50.17] I'd be rollin' on a river with Cree dance\n[00:53.90] Stealin' kisses from Peggy Sue\n[00:57.83] I'd be knee-deep in sand on a Panama beach\n[01:01.41] In the spring of '72\n[01:05.41] I'd be wastin' away on the dock of the bay\n[01:09.59] Watchin' the tide roll in\n[01:12.70] He said, \"What I wouldn't give just to live those songs, again\"\n[01:24.05] Saw him workin' the counter at Walgreens\n[01:27.75] With a new haircut and a Bachelor's Degree\n[01:32.25] Talkin' to himself about his raw deal\n[01:35.95] Cussin' Uncle Sam and the GI bill\n[01:38.98] He said, \"This world ain't the same if you ask me\"\n[01:42.92] If I could be somewhere else, I'd tell you where I'd be\n[01:46.62] I'd be rollin' on a river with Cree dance\n[01:50.43] Stealin' kisses from Peggy Sue\n[01:54.48] I'd be knee-deep in sand on a Panama beach\n[01:58.03] In the spring of '72\n[02:01.90] I'd be wastin' away on the dock of the bay\n[02:06.12] Watchin' the tide roll in\n[02:08.33] He said, What I wouldn't give just to live those songs, again\n[02:28.19] He said, \"This world ain't the same if you ask me\"\n[02:31.87] If I could be somewhere else, I'd tell you where I'd be\n[02:35.66] I'd be rollin' on a river with Cree dance\n[02:39.50] Stealin' kisses from Peggy Sue\n[02:43.33] I'd be knee-deep in sand on a Panama beach\n[02:46.97] In the spring of '72\n[02:50.96] I'd be wastin' away on the dock of the bay\n[02:55.15] Watchin' the tide roll in\n[02:58.23] He said, \"What I wouldn't give just to live those songs, again\"\n[03:09.05] Oh, again\n[03:10.34]",
