        "fullLyrics": "[00:01.290] Getting Ready for the big revival\n[00:16.759] Getting ready for the big revival\n[00:27.099] Getting ready for the big revival\n[00:32.139] Everybody get in the van\n[00:36.749] There's a little church\n[00:37.879] On eagle mountain\n[00:41.889] It's called The blood\n[00:43.109] Of the blessed land\n[00:47.369] If your faith ain't strong enough child\n[00:50.039] You might wind up dead\n[00:52.509] Praise the lord\n[00:53.379] And pass me a copperhead\n[00:59.979] Now reverand Jones\n[01:01.088] He struts some Dances\n[01:05.128] While the guitar plays amazing grace\n[01:10.298] He testifies in tounges of fire\n[01:15.458] With tears of joy running down his face\n[01:20.888] He ain't sure  and we ain't sure\n[01:23.338] Excatly what he said\n[01:25.767] But praise the lord\n[01:27.057] And pass me a copperhead\n[01:33.767] You won't find many hypocrites\n[01:35.856] That will take the chance on getting bit\n[01:38.706] But a true believer can survive\n[01:41.516] Rattlesnakes and cyanide\n[02:09.007] Now I'll bring you home\n[02:10.197] That deadly viper\n[02:14.087] Keep the holy spirit in your mind\n[02:19.617] You might lose your concentration\n[02:24.427] That serpent's surely bound to strike\n[02:29.937] Either way you won't forget\n[02:32.257] The first time that you said\n[02:35.067] Praise the lord\n[02:36.017] And pass me a copperhead\n[02:42.917] Praise the lord\n[02:43.787] And pass me a copperhead",
