        "fullLyrics": "[00:09.00] I'm going under and this time I fear there's no one to save me\n[00:15.73] \n[00:17.87] This all or nothing really got a way of driving me crazy\n[00:24.25] I need somebody to heal, somebody to know\n[00:29.12] Somebody to have, somebody to hold\n[00:33.40] It's easy to say, but it's never the same\n[00:37.96] I guess I kinda liked the way you numbed all the pain\n[00:41.81] Now the day bleeds into nightfall\n[00:46.37] And you're not here to get me through it all\n[00:50.31] I let my guard down, and then you pulled the rug\n[00:55.06] I was getting kinda used to being someone you loved\n[01:01.38] I'm going under and this time I fear there's no one to turn to\n[01:09.89] This all or nothing way of loving got me sleeping without you\n[01:16.57] Now, I need somebody to know, somebody to heal\n[01:21.40] Somebody to have, just to know how it feels\n[01:25.73] It's easy to say, but it's never the same\n[01:30.21] I guess I kinda liked the way you helped me escape\n[01:34.31] Now the day bleeds into nightfall\n[01:38.68] And you're not here to get me through it all\n[01:42.90] I let my guard down, and then you pulled the rug\n[01:47.45] I was getting kinda used to being someone you loved\n[01:53.25] And I tend to close my eyes when it hurts sometimes\n[01:59.55] I fall into your arms\n[02:03.65] I'll be safe in your sound 'til I come back around\n[02:09.08] For now the day bleeds into nightfall\n[02:13.62] And you're not here to get me through it all\n[02:18.02] I let my guard down, and then you pulled the rug\n[02:22.14] I was getting kinda used to being someone you loved\n[02:26.48] But now the day bleeds into nightfall\n[02:31.03] And you're not here to get me through it all\n[02:35.30] I let my guard down, and then you pulled the rug\n[02:39.63] I was getting kinda used to being someone you loved\n[02:43.93] I let my guard down, and then you pulled the rug\n[02:48.78] I was getting kinda used to being someone you loved\n[02:53.50]",
