        "fullLyrics": "[00:10.18] That girl's got her eyes on a fadin' horizon\n[00:14.39] Here come the last line of our favorite song\n[00:19.49] It's the end of an era\n[00:21.89] She's gonna tear up\n[00:23.92] That interstate on her way to Charleston\n[00:28.43] She's gone movin' on\n[00:30.88] Takin' off my leather jacket\n[00:33.75] Gonna drive as far as she can tonight\n[00:36.54] Gonna sleep on the roadside\n[00:38.10] She'll know when our hometown country station turns to static\n[00:43.69] She ain't ever been that far from home\n[00:46.22] But I know she's better off gone\n[00:48.58] Better off, better off gone\n[00:51.05] Better off, better off gone\n[00:52.72] Better off, better off gone\n[00:55.61] Better off, better off gone\n[00:58.32] We all knew that she was too good for Kansas\n[01:02.79] She swears we'll end up together in the end\n[01:07.57] She wouldn't have to say that\n[01:10.05] If she really thought that fact is\n[01:13.45] She ain't comin' back again\n[01:15.82] And she's gone movin' on\n[01:18.65] Takin' off my leather jacket\n[01:22.00] She gonna drive as far as she can tonight\n[01:24.48] Gonna sleep on the roadside\n[01:26.36] She'll know when our hometown country station turns to static\n[01:31.58] She ain't ever been that far from home\n[01:34.04] But I know she's better off gone\n[01:36.58] Better off, better off gone\n[01:38.62] Better off, better off gone\n[01:41.45] Only good thing I ever had\n[01:46.16] Just up and gone away like that\n[01:51.21] I love her enough to not hold on\n[01:55.05] It's gonna break my heart but I'll get along\n[01:59.26] 'Cause she's better off gone\n[02:18.64] She's gone, movin' on\n[02:21.59] Takin' off my leather jacket\n[02:24.35] She gonna drive as far as she can tonight\n[02:26.89] She gonna sleep on the roadside\n[02:28.73] She'll know when our hometown country station turns to static\n[02:33.95] She ain't ever been that far from home\n[02:36.99] But I know she's better off gone\n[02:39.05] Better off, better off gone, better off\n[02:41.93] (I know she's better off gone)\n[02:43.74] Better off, better off gone, better off\n[02:47.18] (She's better off)\n[02:48.65] Better off, better off gone, better off\n[02:52.06] (She's better off gone)\n[02:53.37] Better off, better off gone\n[02:55.53] Better off, better off gone\n[02:57.81]",
