        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:10] Jack met Jenny on the 4th of July\n[00:13] At the street fair underneath the carnival lights\n[00:15] It was love from the second he stuttered through hello\n\n[00:21] Sparks started flying in the summer air\n[00:23] As they danced to the band on the courthouse square\n[00:26] On a clear midwestern night he walked her home\n\n[00:32] Yeah yeah the world keeps spinning round\n[00:37] Like a carousel who knows where they're bound\n[00:42] They might pull through if they're tough enough\n[00:47] Best you can do is just wish em luck\n\n[00:55] The days blew by like the prairie wind\n[00:58] And each day began like a fairytale ends\n[01:01] And Jack started making the big ol' small town plans\n\n[01:05] Jenny started talking bout her Hollywood dreams\n[01:07] But Jack just wanted Jenny more than anything\n[01:11] And late one night it slipped right through his hands\n\n[01:17]Yeah yeah the world keeps spinning round\n[01:21] Like a carousel who knows where they're bound\n[01:26] They might pull through if they're tough enough\n[01:33] Best you can do is just wish em luck\n[01:38] Wish em luck\n\n[01:53] Now Jenny's on the big screen lighting his fuse\n[01:55] Jack's flying rockets up around the moon\n[01:59] Been ten years since that hot July street fair\n\n[02:04] But the stars lined up one more time\n[02:06] Beneath the fireworks in the heartland sky\n[02:08] When Jack turned around to see Jenny standing there\n\n[02:14] Yeah yeah the world keeps spinning round\n[02:18] Like a carousel who knows where they're bound\n[02:23] They might pull through if they're tough enough\n[02:30] Best you can do is just wish em luck\n\n[02:37] Jack met Jenny on the 4th of July\n[02:39] At the street fair underneath the carnival lights\n[02:41] It was love from the second he stuttered through hello",
