        "dateAdded": "2026-05-18T15:32:15.024Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:17.95] She had a cross around her neck\n[00:22.36] And a flower in her hair\n[00:25.21] That I picked from the side of Thomas Drive\n[00:30.57] On our way to the sand\n[00:35.58] We found an old wooden chair\n[00:40.06] Still warm from the sun\n[00:44.25] Pushed it back, gave me a kiss with Bacardi on her lips\n[00:48.73] And I was done\n[00:52.95] And we spent that week wide open\n[00:57.40] Upside down beside the ocean\n[01:01.98] I didn't know where it was goin'\n[01:06.14] Just tryin' to keep my heart on the tracks\n[01:11.19] I should've known that kind of feelin'\n[01:15.04] Would last longer than that week did\n[01:19.59] Blown away and barely breathin'\n[01:23.72] Sunday came and it was over\n[01:28.46] Now she's got me twisted\n[01:31.15] Like an old beach roller coaster\n[01:38.76] The rest of those days\n[01:41.82] Turned into long crazy nights\n[01:46.85] When the music got loud\n[01:48.94] We'd sneak away from the crowd under the boardwalk lights\n[01:55.83] And with all the things we said\n[02:00.04] What I just can't get past\n[02:04.50] Is the way we let it end\n[02:06.91] Now I'm wonderin' where she is\n[02:09.52] Knowin' I can't get that goodbye back\n[02:13.72] We spent that week wide open\n[02:17.13] Upside down beside the ocean\n[02:21.69] I didn't know where it was goin'\n[02:26.09] Just tryin' to keep my heart on the tracks\n[02:31.08] I should've known that kind of feelin'\n[02:35.06] Would last longer than that week did\n[02:39.21] Blown away and barely breathin'\n[02:43.94] When Sunday came and it was over\n[02:48.44] Now she's got me twisted\n[02:51.37] Like an old beach roller coaster\n[02:55.59] She's like a song playin' over and over\n[02:59.78] In my mind, where I still hold her\n[03:04.20] I had the chance and I should've told her\n[03:11.09] When we spent that week wide open\n[03:13.16] Upside down beside the ocean\n[03:19.75] I should've known where it was goin'\n[03:24.29] Still tryin' to keep my heart on the tracks\n[03:28.69] And I should've known that kind of feelin'\n[03:33.13] Would last longer than that week did\n[03:37.60] Blown away and barely breathin'\n[03:41.86] When Sunday came and it was over\n[03:46.29] Now she's got me twisted, yeah, I'm still twisted\n[03:53.37] Like that old beach roller coaster\n[03:59.63] \n[04:02.59] Like that old beach roller coaster\n[04:07.24]",
