        "chorus": "C# G# Fm D# | C# Fm D# 2x C# D#",
        "chorusCue": "",
        "chorusTitle": "CHORUS",
        "dateAdded": "2026-05-25T13:05:50.114Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:11.02] You got a fast car\n[00:13.38] And I want a ticket to anywhere\n[00:15.98] Maybe we make a deal\n[00:18.30] Maybe together we can get somewhere\n[00:21.00] Any place is better\n[00:23.36] Starting from zero, got nothing to lose\n[00:25.73] Maybe we'll make something\n[00:28.26] Me, myself, I got nothing to prove\n[00:35.42] You got a fast car\n[00:37.95] And I got a plan to get us out of here\n[00:40.15] Been working at the convenience store\n[00:42.98] Managed to save just a little bit of money\n[00:45.27] Won't have to drive too far\n[00:47.66] Just across the border and into the city\n[00:50.17] And you and I can both get jobs\n[00:52.76] Finally see what it means to be living\n[00:56.25] \n[00:59.52] See, my old man's got a problem\n[01:02.31] He lived with the bottle, that's the way it is\n[01:04.55] Said his body's too old for working\n[01:07.14] His body's too young to look like his\n[01:09.78] So, Mama went off and left him\n[01:12.05] She wanted more from life than he could give\n[01:14.40] I said, \"Somebody's got to take care of him\"\n[01:17.02] So, I quit school and that's what I did\n[01:24.68] You got a fast car\n[01:26.83] Is it fast enough so we could fly away?\n[01:29.28] Still gotta make a decision\n[01:31.95] Leave tonight, or live and die this way\n[01:35.42] \n[01:37.43] So, I remember when we were driving, driving in your car\n[01:41.57] Speed so fast, I felt like I was drunk\n[01:44.47] City lights laid out before us\n[01:46.45] And your arm felt nice wrapped around my shoulder\n[01:48.76] And I, I had a feeling that I belonged\n[01:54.06] I, I had a feeling I could be someone, be someone, be someone\n[02:01.00] \n[02:06.05] You got a fast car\n[02:08.66] We go cruising, entertain ourselves\n[02:10.82] You still ain't got a job\n[02:13.19] So I work in the market as a checkout girl\n[02:15.93] I know things will get better\n[02:18.25] You'll find work and I'll get promoted\n[02:20.94] And we'll move out of the shelter\n[02:23.39] Buy a bigger house, live in the suburbs\n[02:25.72] \n[02:28.93] So, I remember when we were driving, driving in your car\n[02:32.93] Speed so fast, I felt like I was drunk\n[02:35.64] City lights lay out before us\n[02:37.90] And your arm felt nice wrapped around my shoulder\n[02:40.38] And I, I had a feeling that I belonged\n[02:45.27] I, I had a feeling I could be someone, be someone, be someone\n[02:52.20] \n[02:57.62] You got a fast car\n[02:59.83] I got a job that pays all our bills\n[03:02.42] You stay out drinking late at the bar\n[03:04.61] See more of your friends than you do of your kids\n[03:07.39] I'd always hoped for better\n[03:09.51] Thought maybe together you and me'd find it\n[03:12.33] I got no plans, I ain't going nowhere\n[03:14.87] Take your fast car and keep on driving\n[03:17.98] \n[03:20.25] So, I remember when we were driving, driving in your car\n[03:24.32] Speed so fast, I felt like I was drunk\n[03:27.32] City lights lay out before us\n[03:29.38] And your arm felt nice wrapped around my shoulder\n[03:31.89] And I, I had a feeling that I belonged\n[03:36.60] I, I had a feeling I could be someone, be someone, be someone\n[03:44.10] \n[03:53.83] You got a fast car\n[03:55.96] Is it fast enough, so we could fly away?\n[03:58.56] You still gotta make a decision\n[04:01.19] Leave tonight, or live and die this way\n[04:03.92]",
