        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:06.420] Turn it up\n[00:23.280] Big wheels keep on turning\n[00:28.230] Carry me home to see my kin\n[00:33.000] Singing songs about the southland\n[00:37.920] I miss ole Bam now once again and I think it's a sin, yes\n[00:52.290] Well I heard Mister Young sing about her\n[00:57.450] Well I heard ole Neil put her down\n[01:02.280] Well I hope Neil Young will remember\n[01:07.320] A southern man don't need him around anyhow\n[01:12.210] Sweet home Alabama\n[01:17.220] Where the skies are so blue\n[01:22.080] Sweet home Alabama\n[01:27.060] Lord I'm coming home to you\n[01:41.610] In Birmingham they love the Gov'nor, boo-hoo-hoo\n[01:46.680] Now we all did what we could do\n[01:51.450] Now Watergate does not bother me\n[01:56.670] Does your conscience bother you, tell the truth\n[02:01.500] Sweet home Alabama\n[02:06.570] Where the skies are so blue\n[02:11.400] Sweet home Alabama\n[02:16.380] Lord I'm coming home to you, here I come, Alabama\n[03:09.960] Now Muscle Shoals has got the Swampers\n[03:15.060] And they've been known to pick a song or two, （yes they do）\n[03:19.950] Lord, they get me off so much\n[03:24.600] They pick me up when I'm feeling blue, now how about you\n[03:29.730] Sweet home Alabama\n[03:34.740] Where the skies are so blue\n[03:39.540] Sweet home Alabama\n[03:44.520] Lord I'm coming home to you\n[03:49.350] Sweet home Alabama, oh sweet home\n[03:54.450] Where the skies are so blue, and the Governer's true\n[03:59.250] Sweet home Alabama, loardy\n[04:04.260] Lord I'm coming home to you, yeah, yeah",
        "genre": [
            "Rock"
        ],
