        "fullLyrics": "[00:08.630] Put on my blue suede shoes\n[00:11.460] And I boarded the plane\n[00:14.790] Touched down in the land of the Delta Blues\n[00:18.880] In the middle of the pouring rain\n[00:22.670] W C  Handy -- won't you look down over me\n[00:29.920] Yeah I got a first class ticket\n[00:33.090] But I'm as blue as a boy can be\n[00:36.220] Then I'm walking in Memphis\n[00:40.260] Walking with my feet ten feet off of Beale\n[00:43.930] Walking in Memphis\n[00:47.350] But do I really feel the way I feel\n[00:54.520] Saw the ghost of Elvis\n[00:57.990] On Union Avenue\n[01:00.620] Followed him up to the gates of Graceland\n[01:04.860] Then I watched him walk right through\n[01:08.310] Now security they did not see him\n[01:11.600] They just hovered 'round his tomb\n[01:15.350] But there's a pretty little thing\n[01:17.540] Waiting for the King\n[01:19.350] Down in the Jungle Room\n[01:21.610] Then I'm walking in Memphis\n[01:25.310] Walking with my feet ten feet off of Beale\n[01:29.710] Walking in Memphis\n[01:33.120] But do I really feel the way I feel\n[01:43.000] They've got catfish on the table\n[01:50.570] They've got gospel in the air\n[01:57.630] And Reverend Green be glad to see you\n[02:03.080] When you haven't got a prayer\n[02:11.120] But boy you've got a prayer in Memphis\n[02:20.310] Now Muriel plays piano\n[02:23.380] Every Friday at the Hollywood\n[02:27.330] And they brought me down to see her\n[02:31.170] And they asked me if I would --\n[02:35.430] Do a little number\n[02:38.200] And I sang with all my might\n[02:41.760] And she said --\n[02:42.760] Tell me are you a Christian child\n[02:45.510] And I said Ma'am I am tonight\n[02:48.840] Then I'm walking in Memphis\n[02:52.340] Walking with my feet ten feet off of Beale\n[02:55.830] Walking in Memphis\n[02:59.480] But do I really feel the way I feel\n[03:03.070] Then I'm walking in Memphis\n[03:06.790] Walking with my feet ten feet off of Beale\n[03:10.330] Walking in Memphis\n[03:13.940] But do I really feel the way I feel\n[03:25.090] Put on my blue suede shoes\n[03:28.200] And I boarded the plane\n[03:31.460] Touched down in the land of the Delta Blues\n[03:35.630] In the middle of the pouring rain\n[03:39.030] Touched down in the land of the Delta Blues\n[03:46.170] In the middle of the pouring rain",
