        "chorus": "F#m | A D A E A D | E A D 2x D E",
        "chorusCue": "",
        "chorusTitle": "VERSE",
        "dateAdded": "2026-06-01T13:59:35.866Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:19.36] I am Jeremiah Dixon\n[00:21.77] I am a Geordie Boy\n[00:24.41] A glass of wine with you, sir\n[00:26.58] And the ladies I'll enjoy\n[00:30.65] All Durham and Northumberland\n[00:34.61] Is measured up by my own hand\n[00:39.03] It was my fate from birth\n[00:43.31] To make my mark upon the earth\n[00:49.87] He calls me Charlie Mason\n[00:52.49] A stargazer am I\n[00:55.29] It seems that I was born\n[00:57.39] To chart the evening sky\n[01:00.62] They'd cut me out for baking bread\n[01:05.13] But I had other dreams instead\n[01:09.08] This baker's boy from the west country\n[01:13.35] Would join the Royal Society\n[01:19.74] We are sailing to Philadelphia\n[01:25.70] A world away from the coaly Tyne\n[01:30.39] Sailing to Philadelphia\n[01:35.62] To draw the line\n[01:39.58] The Mason-Dixon line\n[02:05.95] Now you're a good surveyor, Dixon\n[02:08.52] But I swear you'll make me mad\n[02:11.91] The West will kill us both\n[02:13.12] You gullible Geordie lad\n[02:17.29] You talk of liberty\n[02:21.07] How can America be free\n[02:25.65] A Geordie and a baker's boy\n[02:29.95] In the forest of the Iroquois\n[02:36.42] Now hold your head up, Mason\n[02:38.46] See America lies there\n[02:41.91] The morning tide has raised\n[02:43.58] The capes of Delaware\n[02:47.76] Come up and feel the sun\n[02:51.78] A new morning is begun\n[02:56.14] Another day will make it clear\n[03:00.08] Why your stars should guide us here\n[03:06.32] We are sailing to Philadelphia\n[03:12.35] A world away from the coaly Tyne\n[03:16.86] Sailing to Philadelphia\n[03:22.21] To draw the line\n[03:26.15] The Mason-Dixon line\n[03:38.75]",
