        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:32.45] The drinking dens are spilling out, there's staggering in the square\n[00:36.35] There's lads and lasses falling about and a crackling in the air\n[00:40.50] Down around the dungeon doors, the shelters and the queues\n[00:44.46] Everybody's looking for somebody's arms to fall into\n[00:47.80] It's what it is\n[00:51.49] It's what it is now\n[00:55.46] There's frost on the graves and the monuments but the taverns are warm in town\n[01:00.08] People curse the government and shovel hot food down\n[01:03.87] Lights are out in the city hall, the castle and the keep\n[01:07.72] The moon shines down upon it all, the legless and the sleepless\n[01:11.62] Cold on the tollgate\n[01:13.47] With the wagons creeping through\n[01:15.97] Cold on the tollgate\n[01:17.34] God knows what I could do with you\n[01:19.56] It's what it is\n[01:22.71] It's what it is now\n[01:27.06] The Garison sleeps in the citadel with the ghost and the ancient stones\n[01:31.68] High on the parapet, a Scottish piper stands alone\n[01:35.56] High on the wind, the highland drums begin to roll\n[01:39.35] And something from the past just comes and stares into my soul\n[01:43.43] Cold on the tollgate\n[01:44.84] With the Caledonian blues\n[01:47.40] Cold on the tollgate\n[01:48.78] God knows what I could do with you\n[01:50.94] It's what it is\n[01:54.39] It's what it is now\n[01:57.93] What it is\n[02:02.28] It's what it is now\n[02:05.06] \n[02:38.12] There's a chink of light, there's a burning wick, there's a lantern in the tower\n[02:41.96] Wee Willie Winkie with a candlestick still writing songs in the wee wee hours\n[02:46.15] On Charlotte Street, I take a walking stick from my hotel\n[02:50.16] The ghost of Dirty Dick is still in search of Little Nell\n[02:53.92] It's what it is\n[02:57.35] It's what it is now\n[03:01.13] Mh, it's what it is\n[03:05.22] What it is now, now, now\n[03:24.12]",
        "genre": [
            "Rock"
        ],
