        "chorus": "D A Bm G A 4x",
        "chorusCue": "",
        "chorusTitle": "Chorus",
        "dateAdded": "2026-06-09T08:35:32.852Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:12.02] Traveling in a fried-out Kombi\n[00:16.53] On a hippie trail, head full of zombie\n[00:21.49] I met a strange lady, she made me nervous\n[00:25.18] She took me in and gave me breakfast\n[00:29.37] And she said\n[00:30.45] \"Do you come from a land down under\n[00:34.70] Where women glow and men plunder?\n[00:39.43] Can't you hear, can't you hear the thunder?\n[00:42.18] \n[00:44.24] You better run, you better take cover\"\n[00:46.41] \n[00:57.16] Buying bread from a man in Brussels\n[01:01.59] He was six-foot-four and full of muscle\n[01:05.98] I said, \"Do you speak-a my language?\"\n[01:10.30] He just smiled and gave me a Vegemite sandwich\n[01:14.09] And he said\n[01:15.16] \"I come from a land down under\n[01:19.54] Where beer does flow and men chunder\n[01:23.89] Can't you hear, can't you hear the thunder?\n[01:27.99] You better run, you better take cover, yeah\"\n[01:32.07] \n[01:59.13] Lying in a den in Bombay\n[02:03.70] With a slack jaw and not much to say\n[02:08.66] I said to the man, \"Are you trying to tempt me?\n[02:12.79] Because I come from the land of plenty\"\n[02:16.17] And he said\n[02:18.39] Oh, \"Do you come from a land down under? (Oh, yeah-yeah)\n[02:21.84] Where women glow and men plunder?\n[02:26.20] Can't you hear, can't you hear the thunder?\n[02:29.92] You better run, you better take cover\", 'cause we are\n[02:35.39] Living in a land down under\n[02:39.61] Where women glow and men plunder (yeah)\n[02:44.42] Can't you hear, can't you hear the thunder? (Thunder)\n[02:49.20] You better-better run, you better take cover\n[02:52.93] Living in a land down under\n[02:57.55] Where women glow and men plunder\n[03:01.80] Can't you hear, can't you hear the thunder? Ooh, yeah\n[03:06.12] You better run, you better take cover\n[03:10.02] (We are) living in a land down under (ooh, yeah)\n[03:13.85] Where women glow and men plunder\n[03:19.72] Can't you, can't you hear the thunder? (Can't you, can't you hear the thunder?)\n[03:28.56] You better run, you better take cover\n[03:31.20] Living in a land down under (living in a land down under)\n[03:34.39] Where women glow and men plunder\n[03:37.35] Can't you, can't you hear the thunder?\n[03:38.98]",
