        "dateAdded": "2026-04-30T12:47:55.920Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:19.06] I know they say you can't go home again\n[00:26.26] I just had to come back one last time\n[00:31.64] Ma'am, I know you don't know me from Adam\n[00:37.91] But these hand prints on the front steps are mine\n[00:43.37] Up those stairs in that little back bedroom\n[00:48.81] Is where I did my homework and I learned to play guitar\n[00:55.12] And I bet you didn't know under that live oak\n[01:01.44] My favourite dog is buried in the yard\n[01:07.74] I thought if I could touch this place or feel it\n[01:13.21] This brokenness inside me might start healing\n[01:18.65] Out here, it's like I'm someone else\n[01:23.18] I thought that maybe I could find myself\n[01:28.53] If I could just come in, I swear I'll leave\n[01:33.06] Won't take nothin' but a memory\n[01:36.65] From the house that built me\n[01:43.41] \n[01:45.79] Momma cut out pictures of houses for years\n[01:51.12] From better homes and garden magazine\n[01:57.46] Plans were drawn and concrete poured\n[02:00.17] Nail by nail and board by board\n[02:03.75] Daddy gave life to momma's dream\n[02:09.17] I thought if I could touch this place or feel it\n[02:14.60] This brokenness inside me might start healing\n[02:20.97] Out here, it's like I'm someone else\n[02:24.53] I thought that maybe I could find myself\n[02:29.90] If I could just come in, I swear I'll leave\n[02:35.48] Won't take nothin' but a memory\n[02:39.95] From the house that built me\n[02:47.12] You leave home, you move on\n[02:51.60] And you do the best you can\n[02:54.35] I got lost in this whole world\n[02:58.01] And forgot who I am\n[03:02.57] I thought if I could touch this place or feel it\n[03:08.81] This brokenness inside me might start healing\n[03:13.36] Out here, it's like I'm someone else\n[03:17.88] I thought that maybe I could find myself\n[03:24.29] If I could walk around, I swear I'll leave\n[03:28.77] Won't take nothin' but a memory\n[03:32.30] From the house that built me\n[03:37.06]",
        "genre": [
            "Country"
        ],
