        "fullLyrics": "[00:01.950] Look at this photograph\n[00:04.980] Every time I do it makes me laugh\n[00:08.070] How did our eyes get so red\n[00:11.370] And what the hell is on Joey's head?\n[00:15.240] This is where I grew up\n[00:17.940] I think the present owner fixed it up\n[00:21.210] I never knew we ever went without\n[00:24.480] The second floor is hard for sneakin' out\n[00:28.200] And this is where I went to school\n[00:31.020] Most of the time had better things to do\n[00:34.320] Criminal record says I broke in twice\n[00:37.620] I must've done it half a dozen times\n[00:41.340] I wonder if it's too late\n[00:44.100] Should I go back and try to graduate?\n[00:47.430] Life's better now than it was back then\n[00:50.820] If I was them I wouldn't let me in\n[00:54.330] Oh, oh, oh...\n[00:56.760] Oh, God I...\n[00:59.280] Every memory of lookin' out the back door\n[01:02.430] I have the photo album spread out on my bedroom floor\n[01:05.940] It's hard to say it, time to say it\n[01:09.900] Goodbye, goodbye\n[01:12.480] Every memory of walkin' out the front door\n[01:15.540] I found the photo of the friend that I was lookin' for\n[01:19.080] It's hard to say it, time to say it\n[01:23.040] Goodbye, goodbye\n[01:40.440] Remember the old arcade?\n[01:43.350] Blew every dollar that we ever made\n[01:46.620] The cops hated us hangin' out\n[01:49.920] They said somebody went and burned it down\n[01:53.220] We used to listen to the radio\n[01:56.580] And sing along with every song we know\n[01:59.760] We said someday we'd find out how it feels\n[02:03.090] To sing to more than just the steering wheel\n[02:06.780] Kim's the first girl I kissed\n[02:09.750] I was so nervous that I nearly missed\n[02:12.870] She's had a couple of kids since then\n[02:16.260] I haven't seen her since God knows when\n[02:19.830] Oh, oh, oh...\n[02:22.260] Oh, God I...\n[02:24.780] Every memory of lookin' out the back door\n[02:27.900] I have the photo album spread out on my bedroom floor\n[02:31.410] It's hard to say it, time to say it\n[02:35.370] Goodbye, goodbye\n[02:37.950] Every memory of walkin' out the front door\n[02:41.040] I found the photo of the friend that I was lookin' for\n[02:44.550] It's hard to say it, time to say it\n[02:48.510] Goodbye, goodbye\n[02:58.080] I miss that town, I miss the faces\n[03:05.700] You can't erase, you can't replace it\n[03:12.390] I miss it now, I can't believe it\n[03:18.810] So hard to stay, too hard to leave it\n[03:25.740] If I could relive those days\n[03:28.620] I know the one thing that would never change\n[03:33.750] Every memory of lookin' out the back door\n[03:36.930] I have the photo album spread out on my bedroom floor\n[03:40.440] It's hard to say it, time to say it\n[03:44.400] Goodbye, goodbye\n[03:47.010] Every memory of walkin' out the front door\n[03:50.070] I found the photo of the friend that I was lookin' for",
