        "dateAdded": "2026-05-13T10:42:53.811Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:17.24] As you promised me that I was more than all the miles combined\n[00:21.15] You must have had yourself a change of heart like\n[00:24.39] Halfway through the drive\n[00:25.80] Because your voice trailed off exactly as you passed my exit sign\n[00:29.26] Kept on drivin' straight and left our future to the right\n[00:33.74] Now I am stuck between my anger and the blame that I can't face\n[00:36.11] And memories are somethin' even smoking weed does not replace\n[00:42.03] And I am terrified of weather 'cause I see you when it rains\n[00:47.07] Doc told me to travel, but there's COVID on the planes\n[00:50.75] And I love Vermont, but it's the season of the sticks\n[00:54.36] And I saw your mom, she forgot that I existed\n[00:58.71] And it's half my fault, but I just like to play the victim\n[01:02.57] I'll drink alcohol 'til my friends come home for Christmas\n[01:07.01] And I'll dream each night of some version of you\n[01:11.09] That I might not have, but I did not lose\n[01:13.37] Now you're tire tracks and one pair of shoes\n[01:19.28] And I'm split in half, but that'll have to do\n[01:27.37] So I thought that if I piled something good on all my bad\n[01:31.82] That I could cancel out the darkness I inherited from dad\n[01:35.62] No, I am no longer funny, 'cause I miss the way you laugh\n[01:40.17] You once called me forever, now you still can't call me back\n[01:44.07] And I love Vermont, but it's the season of the sticks\n[01:47.14] And I saw your mom, she forgot that I existed\n[01:52.27] And it's half my fault, but I just like to play the victim\n[01:55.21] I'll drink alcohol 'til my friends come home for Christmas\n[01:59.66] And I'll dream each night of some version of you\n[02:03.28] That I might not have, but I did not lose\n[02:07.67] Now you're tire tracks and one pair of shoes\n[02:11.95] And I'm split in half, but that'll have to do\n[02:18.74] Oh, that'll have to do\n[02:23.14] My other half was you\n[02:27.00] I hope this pain's just passin' through\n[02:31.39] But I doubt it\n[02:32.95] And I love Vermont, but it's the season of the sticks\n[02:36.29] And I saw your mom, she forgot that I existed\n[02:41.03] And it's half my fault, but I just like to play the victim\n[02:44.09] I'll drink alcohol 'til my friends come home for Christmas\n[02:48.91] And I'll dream each night of some version of you\n[02:52.77] That I might not have, but I did not lose\n[02:56.06] Now you're tire tracks and one pair of shoes\n[03:01.26] And I'm split in half, but that'll have to do\n[03:05.73] Have to do\n[03:09.76]",
