        "fullLyrics": "[00:11.84] Slip inside the eye of your mind\n[00:15.86] Don't you know you might find\n[00:19.41] A better place to play\n[00:23.66] You said that you'd never been\n[00:27.68] But all the things that you've seen\n[00:31.16] Will slowly fade away\n[00:35.36] So I start a revolution from my bed\n[00:40.94] 'Cause you said the brains I had went to my head\n[00:46.94] Step outside, summertime's in bloom\n[00:52.70] Stand up beside the fireplace\n[00:55.78] Take that look from off your face\n[00:58.74] You ain't ever gonna burn my heart out\n[01:06.51] \n[01:10.29] And so Sally can wait\n[01:14.43] She knows its too late as we're walking on by\n[01:21.88] Her soul slides away\n[01:26.91] \"But don't look back in anger\" I heard you say\n[01:34.29] \n[01:42.76] Take me to the place where you go\n[01:46.85] Where nobody knows if it's night or day\n[01:54.26] Please don't put your life in the hands\n[01:58.42] Of a Rock n' Roll band\n[02:01.95] Who'll throw it all away\n[02:06.13] Gonna start a revolution from my bed\n[02:11.43] 'Cause you said the brains I had went to my head\n[02:17.64] Step outside 'cause summertime's in bloom\n[02:23.31] Stand up beside the fireplace\n[02:26.61] Take that look from off your face\n[02:29.41] 'Cause you ain't ever gonna burn my heart out\n[02:37.40] \n[02:41.12] And so Sally can wait\n[02:45.33] She knows its too late as she's walking on by\n[02:52.59] My soul slides away\n[02:57.88] \"But don't look back in anger\" I heard you say\n[03:08.19] \n[03:39.67] So Sally can wait\n[03:43.95] She knows its too late as we're walking on by\n[03:51.10] Her soul slides away\n[03:56.33] \"But don't look back in anger\" I heard you say\n[04:03.34] So Sally can wait\n[04:07.46] She knows its too late as she's walking on by\n[04:14.79] My soul slides away\n[04:20.29] \"But don't look back in anger, don't look back in anger\"\n[04:28.90] I heard you say\n[04:33.73] \n[04:38.09] At least not today\n[04:41.94]",
