        "dateAdded": "2026-04-24T13:24:25.053Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:12.33] He doesn't fight crime\n[00:15.11] Or wear a cape\n[00:18.52] He doesn't read minds\n[00:21.04] Or levitate\n[00:23.55] But every time my world needs saving\n[00:26.78] He's my Superman\n[00:30.03] Some folks don't believe in heroes\n[00:32.96] 'Cause they haven't met my dad\n[00:48.18] He loves his workshop\n[00:50.28] And rock 'n roll\n[00:53.46] He's got a hot rod\n[00:56.15] And a heart of gold\n[00:58.74] And you could say he's a man of few words\n[01:02.65] But he talks a lot within\n[01:05.26] And even though I'm a little taller\n[01:07.53] I still look up to him\n[01:11.49] He built me a house in the arms of a tree\n[01:15.94] He taught me to drive and to fight and to dream\n[01:21.69] When he looks in my eyes I hope he can see that\n[01:27.56] My dad's a hero to me\n[01:43.91] Rust ridden fenders\n[01:45.74] And doors full of dings\n[01:48.36] Somehow he can fix about anything\n[01:54.86] I didn't think he knew how to cry\n[01:58.64] 'Til our dog died that year\n[02:00.76] He doesn't always say I love you\n[02:03.46] But I can hear him loud and clear\n[02:06.69] He built me a house in the arms of a tree\n[02:11.77] He taught me to drive and to fight and to dream\n[02:16.99] When he looks in my eyes I hope he can see\n[02:23.01] That my dad's a hero to me\n[02:50.14] He built me a house in the arms of a tree\n[02:55.64] He taught me to drive and to fight and to dream\n[03:01.26] When he looks in my eyes I hope he can see\n[03:06.80] That my dad's a hero to me\n[03:12.99] (My dad's a hero)\n[03:15.10] (My dad's a hero)\n[03:17.77] (My dad's a hero)\n[03:20.22] My dad's a hero to me\n[03:23.97] (My dad's a hero)\n[03:26.21] (My dad's a hero)\n[03:30.29] (My dad's a hero)\n[03:31.60] My dad's a hero to me",
