        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:18.83] I went and bought the biggest bottle they got 'cause you're gone\n[00:26.92] Dropped a needle on a vinyl and cried to an old Haggard song\n[00:36.73] Sittin' at the table, baby, breaking the seal\n[00:41.38] Gonna see how much of this pain I can kill\n[00:46.23] I went and bought the biggest bottle they got, 'cause you're gone\n[00:54.30] Tennessee and Kentucky 'cause you ain't here to love me\n[00:59.32] I drink now that there's nothing to lose\n[01:03.53] I've been fightin' with your memory, I hate the way it hits me\n[01:08.48] I wake up every day, black and blue\n[01:12.87] After all this back and forth, a fifth won't do\n[01:21.85] Yeah, I finally got a handle, finally got a handle on you\n[01:28.39] \n[01:36.59] I tell myself that I should quit, but I don't listen to drunks\n[01:45.43] I keep on sippin' 'til, \"I miss you,\" don't roll off my tongue\n[01:54.67] Since you poured our love down the sink\n[01:58.86] I think I'll just stay here and drink\n[02:03.95] I tell myself that I should quit, but I don't listen to drunks\n[02:11.83] Tennessee and Kentucky 'cause you ain't here to love me\n[02:16.96] I drink now that there's nothing to lose\n[02:21.14] I've been fightin' with your memory, I hate the way it hits me\n[02:26.10] I wake up every day, black and blue\n[02:30.76] After all this back and forth, a fifth won't do\n[02:37.37] Well, I finally got a handle on you\n[02:41.22] \n[02:57.71] After all this back and forth, a fifth won't do\n[03:06.98] Yeah, I finally got a handle, finally got a handle on you\n[03:15.65] Handle on you\n[03:18.51] Yeah, I finally got a handle on you\n[03:24.63]",
