        "fullLyrics": "[00:28.679] We skipped the light fandango\n[00:35.039] Turned cartwheels cross the floor\n[00:41.479] I was feeling kind of sea sick\n[00:47.899] The crowd called out for more\n[00:54.379] The room was humming harder\n[01:00.569] As the ceiling flew away\n[01:06.769] When we called out for another drink\n[01:13.249] The waiter brought a tray\n[01:16.969] And so it was that later\n[01:26.179] As the miller told his tale\n[01:32.809] That her face at first just ghostly\n[01:37.439] Turned a whiter shade of pale\n[02:11.838] She said there is no reason\n[02:18.088] And the truth is plain to see\n[02:24.338] That I wandered through my playing cards\n[02:30.918] Would not let her be\n[02:37.028] One of sixteen vestal virgins\n[02:43.638] Who were leaving for the coast\n[02:49.968] And although my eyes were open\n[02:56.438] They might just as well been closed\n[03:00.068] And so it was that later\n[03:09.458] As the miller told his tale\n[03:15.798] That her face at first just ghostly\n[03:20.778] Turned a whiter shade of pale\n[03:51.478] And so it was that later",
