        "fullLyrics": "[00:14.28] I still smell the smoke from the Fourth of July fireworks\n[00:18.83] And I still feel the kick drum front row at the concert\n[00:23.03] After Talladega, safe to say you stick around\n[00:27.78] We were both drunk at the party, when I told you that I loved you\n[00:32.56] You laughed like I was crazy, but I swear, girl that's when I knew\n[00:37.12] What we had, looking back on it right now\n[00:41.57] That last call, first kiss never left my mind\n[00:46.52] That old school Springsteen gets me every time\n[00:50.76] And when I see that leather jacket\n[00:53.40] I think about how you had it\n[00:55.97] Wrapped around your shoulder\n[00:58.23] That whole October\n[01:00.16] And that sunset, barefoot, fire on the beach\n[01:04.76] I can still feel your hands all over me\n[01:09.21] And when the sky lights up\n[01:11.99] Girl, it's your shade of blue\n[01:14.23] 'Cause every other memory\n[01:16.92] Every other memory is you\n[01:23.67] Girl, you're every other turn down every back road in my head\n[01:28.62] And even though it's over, you're still playing hard to forget\n[01:32.63] Close my eyes, and there you are\n[01:35.54] Still underneath the stars\n[01:37.13] 'Cause that last call, first kiss never left my mind\n[01:42.49] That old school Springsteen gets me every time\n[01:46.69] And when I see that leather jacket\n[01:49.49] I think about how you had it\n[01:51.76] Wrapped around your shoulder\n[01:54.06] That whole October\n[01:56.13] And that sunset, barefoot, fire on the beach\n[02:00.84] I can still feel your hands all over me\n[02:05.24] And when the sky lights up\n[02:07.72] Girl, it's your shade of blue\n[02:10.27] 'Cause every other memory\n[02:12.78] Every other memory is you\n[02:18.50] Girl, it's you\n[02:22.15] Every other memory is you and me\n[02:26.60] Wrapped up in the summer\n[02:28.67] There will never be another\n[02:31.46] Never be another\n[02:33.18] Like that last call, first kiss never left my mind\n[02:38.27] And that old school Springsteen gets me every time\n[02:42.33] And when I see that leather jacket\n[02:45.30] I think about how you had it\n[02:47.73] Wrapped around your shoulder\n[02:50.10] That whole October\n[02:52.02] And that sunset, barefoot, fire on the beach\n[02:56.73] I can still feel your hands all over me\n[03:01.14] And when the sky lights up\n[03:03.64] Girl, it's your shade of blue\n[03:06.01] 'Cause every other memory\n[03:08.66] Every other memory is you\n[03:14.48] Girl, it's you\n[03:18.36] Every other memory is you and me\n[03:22.69] Tangled in the summer\n[03:24.67] There will never be another\n[03:27.45] Never be another\n[03:29.38] Like that last call, first kiss\n[03:31.84]",
