        "fullLyrics": "[00:21.93] Mother doesn't know where love has gone\n[00:29.32] She says it must be youth that keeps us feeling strong\n[00:38.03] I see it in her face that's turned to ice\n[00:43.39] And when she smiles, she shows the lines of sacrifice\n[00:51.63] And now I know what they're saying\n[00:55.40] As our sun begins to fade\n[00:59.02] And we made our love on wasteland\n[01:06.23] And through the barricades\n[01:12.58] Father made my history\n[01:16.08] He fought for what he thought would set us somehow free\n[01:24.35] He taught me what to say in school\n[01:29.50] I learned it off by heart but now that's torn in two\n[01:38.14] And now I know what they're saying\n[01:41.57] In the music of the parade\n[01:44.56] And we made our love on wasteland\n[01:51.55] And through the barricades\n[02:07.14] Born on different sides of life\n[02:11.16] But we feel the same and feel all of this strife\n[02:19.84] So come to me when I'm asleep (asleep)\n[02:25.31] And we'll cross the lines and dance upon the streets\n[02:33.97] And now I know what they're saying\n[02:37.48] As the drums begin to fade\n[02:40.11] And we made our love on wasteland\n[02:47.38] And through the barricades\n[02:53.65] Oh, turn around and I'll be there\n[02:57.61] Well, there's a scar right through my heart but I'll bare it again\n[03:04.43] Oh, I thought we were the human race\n[03:08.02] But we were just another borderline case\n[03:12.27] And the stars reach down and tell us\n[03:16.69] That there's always one escape\n[03:22.59] Oh, I don't know where love has gone\n[03:26.29] And in this troubled land desperation keeps us strong\n[03:34.43] Friday's child is full of soul\n[03:39.44] With nothing left to lose, there's everything to go\n[03:49.58] Now I know what they're saying\n[03:53.95] It's a terrible beauty we've made\n[03:56.34] So we make our love on wasteland\n[04:03.31] And through the barricades\n[04:08.10] And now I know what they're saying\n[04:10.53] As our hearts go to their graves\n[04:14.98] And we made our love on wasteland\n[04:22.35] Oh, and through the barricades\n[04:32.22]",
