        "fullLyrics": "[00:12.44] There is a house in New Orleans\n[00:18.01] They call the Rising Sun\n[00:23.91] And it's been the ruin of many poor boys\n[00:30.09] And God, I know I'm one\n[00:35.46] \n[00:46.91] My mother was a tailor\n[00:51.92] She sewed my new blue jeans\n[00:58.00] My father was a gamblin' man\n[01:04.53] Down in New Orleans\n[01:09.81] \n[01:20.26] Now the only thing a gambler needs\n[01:26.20] Is a suitcase and trunk\n[01:32.12] And the only time he's satisfied\n[01:38.52] Is when he's on a drunk\n[01:43.69] \n[02:27.95] Oh, mother, tell your children\n[02:33.32] Not to do what I have done\n[02:39.66] Spend your lives in sin and misery\n[02:45.50] In the house of the rising sun\n[02:50.87] \n[03:01.19] Well, I got one foot on the platform\n[03:07.05] The other foot on the train\n[03:12.98] I'm goin' back to New Orleans\n[03:19.09] To wear that ball and chain\n[03:24.58] \n[03:33.65] Well, there is a house in New Orleans\n[03:39.84] They call the Rising Sun\n[03:46.14] And it's been the ruin of many a poor boys\n[03:52.14] And God, I know I'm one\n[03:55.23]",
