        "dateAdded": "2026-04-30T12:33:29.106Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:02.17] If I die young, bury me in satin\n[00:05.45] Lay me down on a bed of roses\n[00:08.65] Sink me in the river at dawn\n[00:12.71] Send me away with the words of a love song\n[00:16.86] Oh-oh, oh-oh\n[00:22.20] Lord make me a rainbow, I'll shine down on my mother\n[00:28.18] She'll know I'm safe with you when she stands under my colors\n[00:31.06] Oh, and life ain't always what you think it oughta be, no\n[00:36.28] Ain't even gray, but she buries her baby\n[00:39.84] The sharp knife of a short life\n[00:45.78] Well, I've had just enough time\n[00:51.02] If I die young, bury me in satin\n[00:56.55] Lay me down on a bed of roses\n[01:00.26] Sink me in the river at dawn\n[01:03.91] Send me away with the words of a love song\n[01:08.15] The sharp knife of a short life\n[01:15.65] Well, I've had just enough time\n[01:22.43] And I'll be wearing white, when I come into your kingdom\n[01:26.88] I'm as green as the ring on my little cold finger\n[01:30.14] I've never known the lovin' of a man\n[01:33.69] But it sure felt nice when he was holding my hand\n[01:37.42] There's a boy here in town, says he'll love me forever\n[01:41.34] Who would have thought forever could be severed by\n[01:45.58] The sharp knife of a short life\n[01:52.05] Well, I've had just enough time\n[02:01.48] \n[02:14.64] So put on your best boys, and I'll wear my pearls\n[02:19.53] What I never did is done\n[02:23.79] A penny for my thoughts, oh no, I'll sell 'em for a dollar\n[02:28.05] They're worth so much more after I'm a goner\n[02:31.75] And maybe then you'll hear the words I been singing\n[02:35.47] Funny when you're dead how people start listenin'\n[02:42.15] \n[02:48.22] If I die young, bury me in satin\n[02:51.71] Lay me down on a bed of roses\n[02:55.11] Sink me in the river at dawn\n[02:58.84] Send me away with the words of a love song\n[03:03.76] Oh-oh (oh-oh)\n[03:05.92] The ballad of a dove\n[03:07.52] Go with peace and love\n[03:10.93] Gather up your tears, keep 'em in your pocket\n[03:14.41] Save 'em for a time when you're really gonna need 'em oh\n[03:18.97] The sharp knife of a short life\n[03:25.52] Well, I've had just enough time\n[03:32.83] So put on your best boys, and I'll wear my pearls\n[03:40.29]",
