        "fullLyrics": "[00:49.51] Another head hangs lowly\n[00:54.14] Child is slowly taken\n[00:58.59] \n[01:00.86] And the violence caused such silence\n[01:06.02] Who are we mistaken?\n[01:10.92] But you see, it's not me, it's not my family\n[01:16.74] In your head, in your head they are fighting\n[01:22.41] With their tanks, and their bombs, and their bombs, and their guns\n[01:28.47] In your head, in your head they are crying\n[01:34.62] In your head, in your head\n[01:39.83] Zombie, zombie, zombie-ie-ie\n[01:45.83] What's in your head? In your head?\n[01:51.58] Zombie, zombie, zombie-ie-ie-ie, oh\n[01:58.66] Du-du-du-du\n[02:01.60] Du-du-du-du\n[02:04.65] Du-du-du-du\n[02:07.60] Du-du-du-du\n[02:10.37] \n[02:22.27] Another mother's breaking\n[02:26.98] Heart is taking over\n[02:33.58] When the violence causes silence\n[02:38.41] We must be mistaken\n[02:43.63] It's the same old theme, since 1916\n[02:48.87] In your head, in your head they're still fighting\n[02:54.96] With their tanks, and their bombs, and their bombs, and their guns\n[03:00.76] In your head, in your head they are dying\n[03:06.81] In your head, in your head\n[03:12.24] Zombie, zombie, zombie-ie-ie\n[03:17.92] What's in your head? In your head?\n[03:23.57] Zombie, zombie, zombie-ie-ie-ie, oh\n[03:30.61] Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, eh-eh-oh, ra-ra-ra\n[03:42.19]",
