        "fullLyrics": "[00:22.34] Runnin' round in this new truck, bank let's me borrow from month to month\n[00:28.12] Runnin' out of credit and find a little cash on the radio\n[00:33.51] Standin' still they're blowin past, numbers on cars goin' NASCAR fast\n[00:39.66] What I wouldn't give for a slow down, don't ya know\n[00:44.06] 'Cause where I come from only the horses run\n[00:50.35] When the day is done, we take it easy\n[00:55.51] Meanwhile back at Mama's, the porch light's on, come in if you wanna\n[01:01.57] Supper's on the stove and beers in the fridge, red sun sinkin' out low on the ridge,\n[01:07.22] Games on the tube and Daddy smokes cigarettes, whiskey keeps his whistle wet\n[01:12.79] Funny the things you thought you'd never miss, in a world gone crazy as this\n[01:27.03] Well I found a girl and we don't fit in here\n[01:32.02] Talk about how hard it is to breathe here\n[01:34.97] Even with the windows down can't catch a southern breeze here\n[01:37.79] One of these days gonna pack it up and leave here ---\n[01:43.50] 'Cause meanwhile back at Mama's, the porch light's on, come on in if you wanna\n[01:48.71] Supper's on the stove and beers in the fridge, red sun sinkin' out low on the ridge\n[01:54.42] Games on the tube and Daddy smokes cigarettes, whiskey keeps his whistle wet\n[01:59.92] Funny the things you thought you'd never miss, in a world gone crazy as this\n[02:27.10] Oh, I miss yeah a little dirt on the road I miss corn growin' in a row\n[02:32.90] I miss being somebody everybody knows there everybody knows everybody\n[02:38.36] I miss those small town roots, walkin' around in muddy boots\n[02:43.86] The sound of rain on an old tin roof, it's time we head on back ---\n[02:51.74] 'Cause meanwhile back at Mama's the for sale sign's goin' up\n[02:57.71] And I'm gonna dump this truck and the little I got on a loan to own and a three-acre lot\n[03:03.47] Put supper on the stove and beer in the fridge, goin' for broke and we're gonna be rich\n[03:09.21] Watch the sun settin' on the ridge, baby, tell me what you think about this ---\n[03:17.52] Me and you back at Mama's\n[03:28.84] Yeah, me and you back at Mama's\n[03:38.44]",
        "genre": [
            "Country"
        ],
