        "fullLyrics": "[00:08.39] Hank Williams sang it, Number Three drove it\n[00:12.88] Chuck Berry twanged it, Will Faulkner wrote it\n[00:17.10] Aretha Franklin sold it, Dolly Parton graced it\n[00:21.29] Rosa Parks rode it, Scarlett O. chased it\n[00:26.46] Smooth as the hickory wind\n[00:29.74] That blows from Memphis down to Apalachicola\n[00:34.19] It's, \"Hi y'all, did ya eat well?\n[00:38.39] Come on in, I'm sure glad to know ya\"\n[00:43.63] Don't let this old gold cross\n[00:46.60] And this Allman Brothers t-shirt throw ya\n[00:50.76] It's cicadas making noise\n[00:53.89] With the Southern voice\n[00:59.90] \n[01:08.57] Hank Aaron smacked it, Michael Jordan dunked it\n[01:12.90] Pocahontas tracked it, Jack Daniels drunk it\n[01:17.14] Tom Petty rocked it, Dr. King paved it\n[01:21.31] Bear Bryant won it, Billy Graham saved it\n[01:26.21] Smooth as the hickory wind\n[01:29.39] That blows from Memphis down to Apalachicola\n[01:34.71] It's, 'Hi y'all, did ya eat well?\n[01:37.92] Come on in, I'm sure glad to know ya\"\n[01:43.30] Don't let this old gold cross\n[01:46.53] And this Crimson Tide t-shirt throw ya\n[01:50.55] It's cicadas making noise\n[01:54.10] With the Southern voice\n[01:59.86] \n[02:17.52] Jesus is my friend, America is my home\n[02:25.82] Sweet iced tea and Jerry Lee\n[02:29.65] Daytona Beach, that's what gets to me\n[02:33.72] I can feel it in my bones\n[02:39.06] Smooth as the hickory wind\n[02:42.11] That blows from Memphis down to Apalachicola\n[02:47.49] It's, 'Hi y'all, did ya eat well?\n[02:51.85] Come on in, I'm sure glad to know ya\"\n[02:56.28] Don't let this old gold cross\n[02:59.49] And this Charlie Daniels t-shirt throw ya\n[03:03.85] We're just boys making noise\n[03:07.24] With the Southern voice, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah\n[03:16.44] Southern voice\n[03:19.94] I got a Southern voice\n[03:24.64] Southern voice\n[03:30.88]",
