        "dateAdded": "2026-05-17T18:18:34.788Z",
        "externalUrl": "",
        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:12.91] Eddie waited 'til he finished high school\n[00:17.75] He went to Hollywood, got a tattoo\n[00:23.88] He met a girl out there with a tattoo too\n[00:28.73] The future was wide open\n[00:38.99] They moved into a place they both could afford\n[00:44.55] He found a nightclub, he could work at the door\n[00:50.46] She had a guitar and she taught him some chords\n[00:55.61] The sky was the limit\n[01:07.68] Into the great wide open\n[01:13.47] Under them skies of blue\n[01:18.99] Out in the great wide open\n[01:24.71] A rebel without a clue\n[01:49.00] The papers said Ed always played from the heart\n[01:54.32] He got an agent and a roadie named Bart\n[02:00.09] They made a record, and it went in the charts\n[02:05.66] The sky was the limit\n[02:15.02] His leather jacket had chains that would jingle\n[02:20.83] They both met movie stars, partied and mingled\n[02:26.75] Their A&R man said, \"I don't hear a single\"\n[02:32.00] The future was wide open\n[02:43.81] Into the great wide open\n[02:49.04] Under them skies of blue\n[02:55.50] Out in the great wide open\n[03:01.04] A rebel without a clue\n[03:07.52] Into the great wide open\n[03:12.97] Under them skies of blue\n[03:18.81] Into the great wide open\n[03:24.53] A rebel without a clue\n[03:35.72]",
