        "fullLyrics": "[00:20.29] I can't believe the news today\n[00:24.69] Oh, I can't close my eyes and make it go away\n[00:28.62] How long, how long must we sing this song?\n[00:34.83] How long? How long?\n[00:40.49] 'Cause tonight\n[00:43.55] We can be as one\n[00:45.64] Tonight\n[00:50.80] Broken bottles under children's feet\n[00:55.89] Bodies strewn across the dead-end street\n[01:00.62] But I won't heed the battle call\n[01:05.28] It puts my back up, puts my back up against the wall\n[01:10.65] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[01:15.23] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[01:19.81] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[01:22.62] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[01:28.49] Alright, let's go\n[01:31.06] \n[01:40.07] And the battle's just begun\n[01:44.25] There's many lost, but tell me who has won?\n[01:49.24] The trenches dug within our hearts\n[01:53.71] And mothers, children, brothers, sisters torn apart\n[01:57.45] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[02:02.20] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[02:07.18] How long, how long must we sing this song?\n[02:12.36] How long? How long?\n[02:18.38] 'Cause tonight we can be as one, tonight\n[02:28.15] Tonight, tonight (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[02:32.58] Tonight, tonight (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[02:37.43] Alright, let's go\n[02:40.09] \n[03:01.25] Wipe the tears from your eyes\n[03:05.56] Wipe your tears away\n[03:10.11] I'll wipe your tears away\n[03:14.85] I'll wipe your tears away (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[03:20.05] I'll wipe your bloodshot eyes (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[03:26.43] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[03:28.88] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[03:32.45] \n[03:35.84] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[03:37.89] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[03:43.08] \n[03:55.82] And it's true we are immune\n[03:59.24] When fact is fiction and TV reality\n[04:04.18] And today the millions cry (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[04:09.15] We eat and drink while tomorrow they die (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[04:14.03] The real battle just begun (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[04:18.23] To claim the victory Jesus won (Sunday, Bloody Sunday)\n[04:22.78] On Sunday, Bloody Sunday, yeah\n[04:27.95] Sunday, Bloody Sunday\n[04:30.80]",
