        "favorite": false,
        "fullLyrics": "[00:15.63] I got my toes in the water, ass in the sand\n[00:20.37] Not a worry in the world, a cold beer in my hand\n[00:21.90] Life is good today, life is good today\n[00:25.97] Well, the plane touched down just about three o'clock and the city's still on my mind\n[00:33.39] Bikinis and palm trees danced in my head, I was still in the baggage line\n[00:41.02] Concrete and cars are their own prison bars like this life I'm living in\n[00:46.08] But the plane brought me farther, I'm surrounded by water and I'm not going back again\n[00:55.00] I got my toes in the water, ass in the sand\n[00:59.06] Not a worry in the world, a cold beer in my hand\n[01:03.35] Life is good today\n[01:06.66] Life is good today\n[01:08.78] Adiós and vaya con Dios\n[01:14.18] Yeah, I'm leaving GA\n[01:18.75] And if it weren't for tequila and pretty señoritas\n[01:23.48] I'd have no reason to stay\n[01:27.48] Adiós and vaya con Dios\n[01:31.09] Yeah, I'm leaving GA\n[01:35.34] Gonna lay in the hot sun and roll a big fat one\n[01:39.74] And grab my guitar and play\n[01:44.43] \n[01:56.19] Four days flew by like a drunk Friday night\n[01:59.46] As the summer drew to an end\n[02:03.42] They can't believe that I just couldn't leave\n[02:06.88] And I bid adieu to my friends\n[02:10.13] 'Cause my bartender, she's from the islands\n[02:12.77] Her body's been kissed by the sun\n[02:18.11] And coconut replaces the smell of the bar\n[02:20.47] And I don't know if it's her or the rum\n[02:25.14] I got my toes in the water, ass in the sand\n[02:29.17] Not a worry in the world, a cold beer in my hand\n[02:33.17] Life is good today\n[02:35.41] Life is good today\n[02:39.29] Adiós and vaya con Dios\n[02:43.84] A long way from GA\n[02:47.53] Yes, and all the muchachas, they call me big papa\n[02:51.88] When I throw pesos their way\n[02:55.82] Adiós and vaya con Dios\n[02:59.84] A long way from GA\n[03:03.54] Someone do me a favor and pour me some Jaeger and\n[03:08.54] I'll grab my guitar and play\n[03:12.70] \n[03:25.30] Adiós and vaya con Dios\n[03:29.29] Going home now to stay\n[03:33.99] The señoritas don't care-o when there's no dinero\n[03:37.96] Yeah, I got no money to stay\n[03:41.56] Adiós and vaya con Dios\n[03:45.54] Going home now to stay\n[03:49.84] I'm just going to drive up by the lake\n[03:54.25] And put my ass in a lawn chair, toes in the clay\n[03:57.62] Not a worry in the world, a PBR on the way\n[04:01.57] Life is good today\n[04:03.98] Life is good today\n[04:05.90] Rrrah\n[04:06.34]",
